WEBVTT

1
00:01:32,417 --> 00:01:35,750
Hey, Joey. What'd your nonna
send you in here for today, huh?

2
00:01:36,333 --> 00:01:38,500
Two loaves of bread and a dozen zeppole.

3
00:01:38,583 --> 00:01:41,708
Zeppoles are hot and fresh.
They're coming right up, my friend.

4
00:01:42,208 --> 00:01:44,458
Be good. Say the rosary.

5
00:01:44,542 --> 00:01:47,958
Now, Joey,
don't eat 'em all before you get home.

6
00:01:50,542 --> 00:01:51,917
Play ball!

7
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,875
I love your new car, Mr. Romano.
It's a classic.

8
00:01:54,958 --> 00:01:56,667
Ah, thank you, Joe.

9
00:01:57,292 --> 00:01:59,000
- Hey, Joey.
- Hey, Bruno.

10
00:01:59,083 --> 00:02:01,208
Bruno. You missed a spot.

11
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,208
Get in there.

12
00:02:24,417 --> 00:02:25,792
Mamma, I got the bread.

13
00:02:26,542 --> 00:02:28,375
Bravo, Joey.

14
00:02:28,458 --> 00:02:29,667
Zeppole.

15
00:02:31,875 --> 00:02:33,167
Joey!

16
00:02:33,250 --> 00:02:34,792
No zeppole.

17
00:02:34,875 --> 00:02:36,333
Get outta here.

18
00:03:03,958 --> 00:03:06,917
Joey, do you wanna come
see Nonna make the gravy?

19
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:08,875
Vieni cà.

20
00:03:15,958 --> 00:03:17,958
Guarda, aspetta.

21
00:03:19,083 --> 00:03:20,083
Smell.

22
00:03:24,792 --> 00:03:28,167
- How do you know how much to use?
- You feel in your heart.

23
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:29,875
You put in your heart.

24
00:03:36,083 --> 00:03:37,083
Mangia.

25
00:03:40,833 --> 00:03:42,125
It's perfect, Nonna.

26
00:03:42,208 --> 00:03:45,042
No. You areperfecto.

27
00:03:49,208 --> 00:03:52,500
- "One does not grow old at the table."
- Mm-hm.

28
00:04:03,708 --> 00:04:05,458
Hey! Get outta here!

29
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:11,292
- You like the lasagne?
- Who took all the corner pieces?

30
00:04:13,167 --> 00:04:14,875
Hey, what happened to the lasagne?

31
00:04:15,917 --> 00:04:18,583
- Do you call it sauce or gravy?
- Sauce.

32
00:04:27,417 --> 00:04:28,417
Mm!

33
00:04:28,958 --> 00:04:29,958
Mamma.

34
00:04:30,042 --> 00:04:32,417
- Hey!
- Ah!

35
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:35,458
- Roberta! Oh my gosh!
- Ciao, Roberta!

36
00:04:35,958 --> 00:04:37,375
Hey!

37
00:04:37,458 --> 00:04:39,125
Roberta!

38
00:04:47,375 --> 00:04:49,042
Fotografia!

39
00:04:49,125 --> 00:04:50,750
No!

40
00:05:21,708 --> 00:05:24,208
- Hey.
- Oh, I'm sorry for your loss, Joey.

41
00:05:24,875 --> 00:05:26,875
Your mother had a heart of gold.

42
00:05:27,667 --> 00:05:32,667
I made you stuffed shells
with fresh ricotta and spinach for later.

43
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:34,167
Thank you.

44
00:05:48,292 --> 00:05:50,042
To your ma, Maria.

45
00:05:51,042 --> 00:05:52,417
She was like my mother.

46
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:54,917
- Only nice.
- Yeah.

47
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,375
- Salute.
- Salute.

48
00:05:57,083 --> 00:05:58,417
Hmm.

49
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:06,375
I don't know what, uh, tomorrow
is supposed to look like, Bruno, you know?

50
00:06:09,542 --> 00:06:11,250
- Give it time.
- Yeah.

51
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,750
Gets better with time.

52
00:06:16,750 --> 00:06:18,792
That wife of mine
just gave me the stink eye?

53
00:06:18,875 --> 00:06:20,958
Yeah. Looks that way.

54
00:06:22,042 --> 00:06:23,167
Here we go.

55
00:06:23,667 --> 00:06:26,708
- Joe, I made you my scungilli.
- I told you he didn't like scungilli.

56
00:06:26,792 --> 00:06:29,167
Would you shut up? You got a loud mouth.

57
00:06:29,917 --> 00:06:32,208
You need to feed your grief.
It's the only way through.

58
00:06:32,292 --> 00:06:33,125
Mm-hmm.

59
00:06:33,208 --> 00:06:35,375
There's 18 cloves of garlic in there.

60
00:06:35,875 --> 00:06:37,167
Thank you.

61
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:39,750
- I'll come by this week, okay?
- Okay.

62
00:06:42,875 --> 00:06:45,833
I want you to take these and eat them.

63
00:06:45,917 --> 00:06:47,917
Your famous cassatas.

64
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,375
Here, please.

65
00:06:50,167 --> 00:06:51,167
Hmm.

66
00:06:51,625 --> 00:06:53,375
- Delicious.
- Prego.

67
00:06:53,458 --> 00:06:56,833
- You were one of my mom's favorites, Gia.
- Well, 26 years.

68
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:59,208
She was more than a client.
She was a friend.

69
00:06:59,292 --> 00:07:02,083
I just wanna say thank you for everything.

70
00:07:02,167 --> 00:07:03,708
You made her that beautiful wig.

71
00:07:03,792 --> 00:07:08,250
Yeah, well, we all deserve our dignity,
especially at the end.

72
00:07:09,292 --> 00:07:11,875
You know, if you need anything,
you know where to find me.

73
00:07:11,958 --> 00:07:12,958
Yeah.

74
00:07:13,667 --> 00:07:14,833
Okay.

75
00:07:14,917 --> 00:07:16,667
- Refrigerate those.
- Yes.

76
00:07:19,042 --> 00:07:20,917
Next Sunday, dinner.

77
00:07:21,792 --> 00:07:23,833
- That wasn't a question.
- Yeah.

78
00:07:23,917 --> 00:07:24,958
Okay.

79
00:07:28,167 --> 00:07:29,917
Oh, wow.

80
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,375
- She looks beautiful, Bruno.
- Thanks to you.

81
00:07:32,458 --> 00:07:34,333
Please. I love working on her.

82
00:07:34,417 --> 00:07:37,958
Madone, the way you talk about this car,
I swear you'd marry this car if you could.

83
00:07:38,042 --> 00:07:39,875
All right, all right. In, get in.

84
00:07:40,792 --> 00:07:42,458
She's right. I'd marry the car.

85
00:07:42,542 --> 00:07:44,375
I heard that!

86
00:07:45,833 --> 00:07:48,125
Boy, a lot of good memories in there.

87
00:07:48,208 --> 00:07:50,625
Remember my dad with the goddamn hubcaps?

88
00:07:53,583 --> 00:07:54,792
Sucks losing 'em.

89
00:07:55,917 --> 00:07:57,083
Yeah.

90
00:07:57,875 --> 00:07:59,250
Call you tomorrow.

91
00:07:59,958 --> 00:08:00,958
Yeah.

92
00:08:01,292 --> 00:08:03,208
Yep.

93
00:09:10,167 --> 00:09:12,208
Mi disgusta!

94
00:09:12,292 --> 00:09:13,812
- Where's the oregano?
- Roberta, please.

95
00:09:13,875 --> 00:09:16,042
- You call this Italian food?
- All right, all right.

96
00:09:16,125 --> 00:09:17,250
- Joe!
- Come on, Roberta.

97
00:09:17,333 --> 00:09:18,458
She's attacking me again.

98
00:09:18,542 --> 00:09:21,125
- Roberta, come on.
- He calls this spaghetti and meatballs?

99
00:09:21,208 --> 00:09:23,375
- It's deli meat and ketchup!
- Hey!

100
00:09:23,958 --> 00:09:25,958
This is good stuff. See?

101
00:09:27,125 --> 00:09:29,792
- Hey! Come on, stop.
- Get outta here!

102
00:09:29,875 --> 00:09:32,917
Il diavolo! He's trying to kill me!

103
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,417
I want to kill you.

104
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:37,375
- Hope the family's good. Nice to see you.
- Good to see you, Joe.

105
00:09:37,458 --> 00:09:40,917
- I know what you're gonna say.
- What? Stop abusing the chef?

106
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,792
- Abuse? Abuse the chef?
- Yeah.

107
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:47,482
The police are coming.
They got an assault charge against you.

108
00:09:47,542 --> 00:09:50,917
Yeah, well, when my foot
gets better, he'll see abuse.

109
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,000
My foot right up hisculo.

110
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:57,042
Hey, I got something for you.

111
00:09:57,542 --> 00:09:58,667
What?

112
00:10:02,375 --> 00:10:05,208
She wanted to make sure
that I got this to you.

113
00:10:17,708 --> 00:10:19,625
I couldn't, Joey. I…

114
00:10:19,708 --> 00:10:21,500
I'm sorry, I…

115
00:10:22,667 --> 00:10:25,750
I just couldn't bring myself
to go to her funeral.

116
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:26,833
I know.

117
00:10:26,917 --> 00:10:28,083
Hey, it's okay.

118
00:10:28,167 --> 00:10:29,458
It's okay.

119
00:10:30,417 --> 00:10:33,542
For 60 years, she was my best friend.

120
00:10:34,750 --> 00:10:35,833
And you were hers.

121
00:10:37,125 --> 00:10:41,583
You know, you just can't say goodbye
to someone after 60 years.

122
00:10:41,667 --> 00:10:43,333
It's just not possible.

123
00:10:45,125 --> 00:10:47,500
She knew I loved this pin.

124
00:10:48,292 --> 00:10:50,208
Come on, let's make... Put it on.

125
00:10:51,333 --> 00:10:52,542
Be nice.

126
00:10:54,417 --> 00:10:55,667
That's good.

127
00:10:57,292 --> 00:10:59,500
I think it looks nice. Hmm?

128
00:11:00,875 --> 00:11:02,750
Oh. Wait a minute.

129
00:11:06,333 --> 00:11:08,542
I almost forgot.

130
00:11:10,708 --> 00:11:12,625
It's a letter from your mom.

131
00:11:19,583 --> 00:11:20,583
That's nice.

132
00:11:23,625 --> 00:11:25,583
You'll know when you're ready.

133
00:11:26,417 --> 00:11:28,000
And you'll open it then.

134
00:11:29,875 --> 00:11:31,042
Thank you.

135
00:11:37,625 --> 00:11:39,833
"One does not grow old at the table."

136
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:47,417
Hey, there he is!

137
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:48,875
The legend returns!

138
00:11:49,458 --> 00:11:52,333
From the look of the outside,
it's probably just a battery line.

139
00:11:52,417 --> 00:11:54,542
Should be a pretty quick fix this morning.

140
00:11:54,625 --> 00:11:56,500
Are you trying to make the bus bad?

141
00:11:56,583 --> 00:11:58,083
- It looks good.
- What is going on?

142
00:11:58,667 --> 00:12:01,042
Better punch in quick.
Boss has been on the warpath.

143
00:12:01,125 --> 00:12:03,208
Good to know nothing's changed.

144
00:12:03,292 --> 00:12:07,333
- What's that? Smells good.
- Something I brought for the break room.

145
00:12:07,417 --> 00:12:11,042
My nonna'spolpette,
or as close as I could possibly get to it.

146
00:12:11,125 --> 00:12:14,208
Anyway, thanks for coming last week.
I appreciate you guys.

147
00:12:14,292 --> 00:12:17,625
Hey, no matter how old you are,
there's nothing worse than losing your ma.

148
00:12:21,083 --> 00:12:22,958
Hi, Mr. McClane. Good morning.

149
00:12:23,042 --> 00:12:25,542
- Good to see you.
- Joe! Good to see you.

150
00:12:25,625 --> 00:12:27,542
Got worried when you took
so many vacation days.

151
00:12:27,625 --> 00:12:30,542
- Thought you'd never come back.
- No, that would never happen.

152
00:12:31,042 --> 00:12:32,625
Good to be back. And, um…

153
00:12:32,708 --> 00:12:37,708
Gosh, thank you so much
for remembering me with the fruit basket.

154
00:12:37,792 --> 00:12:40,250
- You got it.
- Tangerines and stuff. Thank you for that.

155
00:12:40,333 --> 00:12:44,583
Of course. I lost my cat last year,
so I understand the grieving process.

156
00:12:44,667 --> 00:12:46,333
It's the least I could do.

157
00:12:48,417 --> 00:12:50,542
Sorry about your cat. I didn't know.

158
00:12:52,833 --> 00:12:53,875
Break's over.

159
00:12:55,125 --> 00:12:56,000
Okay.

160
00:12:56,083 --> 00:12:58,292
- Okay.
- Thank you again.

161
00:12:58,958 --> 00:13:02,042
Joe, when I said Sunday dinner,
I didn't mean for you to cook for us.

162
00:13:02,125 --> 00:13:04,750
Oh, stop it. I love having you guys here.

163
00:13:04,833 --> 00:13:08,083
Okay. This is my nonna's.
It's a homemade pasta.

164
00:13:08,167 --> 00:13:10,875
It's got pork cheek, Pecorino cheese,

165
00:13:11,458 --> 00:13:16,583
and vine-ripened San Marzano tomatoes
for the pomodoro sauce.

166
00:13:17,292 --> 00:13:20,417
- Well, I'm impressed.
- Since when are you so into cooking?

167
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:24,542
I don't know. Lately, I've been going
through all my ma and nonna's dishes,

168
00:13:24,625 --> 00:13:27,792
the ones that I remember,
and just making them one by one.

169
00:13:27,875 --> 00:13:31,417
I've gotten close on a few,
but it's my nonna's Sunday gravy.

170
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:34,208
I really wish I could figure
that one out. Anyway…

171
00:13:34,292 --> 00:13:36,542
- Buon appetito.
- Well, it looks delicious.

172
00:13:36,625 --> 00:13:37,708
Salute. Let's eat.

173
00:13:37,792 --> 00:13:38,917
Look…

174
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,458
Just… Joe, before we eat,

175
00:13:41,542 --> 00:13:44,708
there is something
Bruno and I wanna talk to you about.

176
00:13:44,792 --> 00:13:47,458
She's very worried.
I hear about it 50 times a day.

177
00:13:47,542 --> 00:13:50,833
Since your mother's gone,
I'm just worried about your future.

178
00:13:50,917 --> 00:13:54,625
I mean, you took care of her for so long,
and it was beautiful,

179
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:57,000
but now it's time for you
to take care of you.

180
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,167
What does that even mean? I…

181
00:14:00,833 --> 00:14:03,375
- Maybe you could chime in.
- All right, fine.

182
00:14:03,458 --> 00:14:06,625
We're not kids anymore, right?
You need a plan.

183
00:14:07,833 --> 00:14:11,583
- Take your mother's insurance.
- I don't even wanna talk about that.

184
00:14:11,667 --> 00:14:16,042
I had to lose her to get the money...
It's not how I wanna spend my night…

185
00:14:16,125 --> 00:14:20,458
I know... Joe, but the way
to honor her is to spend it.

186
00:14:20,542 --> 00:14:25,417
Find something that makes you really happy
or something that makes you feel her.

187
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:27,917
Or take care of your debt.

188
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,708
$200,000 goes a long way.

189
00:14:29,792 --> 00:14:31,917
- Okay.
- I don't know, maybe it's...

190
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,542
Maybe it's buying some new clothes

191
00:14:33,625 --> 00:14:36,708
or, um, some furniture.
I mean, that chair.

192
00:14:36,792 --> 00:14:39,458
Madone, that was Bruno's
before we were married.

193
00:14:39,542 --> 00:14:43,458
- I like it. What's wrong with it?
- Great for watching Yankee games.

194
00:14:43,542 --> 00:14:46,375
Shaped like a baseball glove.
100% Corinthian leather.

195
00:14:46,458 --> 00:14:47,792
Okay, okay, maybe, I don't know.

196
00:14:47,875 --> 00:14:50,434
Maybe a hobby. I have a friend
who just took up flamenco dancing.

197
00:14:50,458 --> 00:14:54,667
Oh, stop it with the flamenco dancing.
He's not going flamenco dancing.

198
00:14:54,750 --> 00:14:56,292
What about volleyball? You like it.

199
00:14:56,375 --> 00:14:59,167
I guess. I don't know.
You mean, to play the volleyball?

200
00:14:59,250 --> 00:15:02,625
I don't care what you do.
You gotta try something new.

201
00:15:02,708 --> 00:15:06,083
If you keep doing the same thing,
the same is gonna keep happening.

202
00:15:06,167 --> 00:15:10,417
I don't want you sitting in that
damn chair when you're 60.Capisce?

203
00:15:13,042 --> 00:15:15,208
- Capisce.
- I'm sorry I'm nagging, just…

204
00:15:15,292 --> 00:15:17,708
I worry because I love you.

205
00:15:17,792 --> 00:15:19,208
- No, I know.
- Okay.

206
00:15:19,292 --> 00:15:21,000
- I love you. Thank you.
- Okay.

207
00:15:21,667 --> 00:15:23,958
- Okay.
- I love you too.

208
00:15:24,042 --> 00:15:26,750
And I'm also very hungry, so let's eat.

209
00:15:26,833 --> 00:15:30,583
- Nothing worse than a cold pork cheek.
- I'm excited for you to try this. Okay.

210
00:16:25,708 --> 00:16:26,875
Hi, how are you?

211
00:16:37,958 --> 00:16:39,250
Bellissimo.

212
00:16:52,333 --> 00:16:53,458
Hmm.

213
00:16:54,375 --> 00:16:56,167
- This is a nice one.
- Yeah.

214
00:16:57,292 --> 00:17:00,458
My nonna used to do
the exact same thing with the…

215
00:17:00,542 --> 00:17:03,583
Well, I mean,
the tomato's the heart of your dish.

216
00:17:03,667 --> 00:17:06,167
- Don't have heart, don't have nothing.
- True story.

217
00:17:07,292 --> 00:17:09,917
Okay, give me, uh, three of these.

218
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,292
- Three. Anything for you.
- Grazie.

219
00:17:12,375 --> 00:17:14,792
- Prego.
- Okay, Antonella, I got the flowers.

220
00:17:14,875 --> 00:17:17,458
- Oh, good. Oh, they're beautiful.
- Olivia?

221
00:17:19,083 --> 00:17:19,917
Joe?

222
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,333
- Oh, my gosh. You look exactly the same.
- What?

223
00:17:22,417 --> 00:17:24,958
Oh, come on. This is crazy.

224
00:17:25,042 --> 00:17:27,083
- I mean it.
- Like, been 30 years.

225
00:17:27,167 --> 00:17:29,250
No, I swear to God,
you haven't changed at all.

226
00:17:29,333 --> 00:17:30,534
- You look terrific.
- Thank you.

227
00:17:30,583 --> 00:17:31,958
You know this man?

228
00:17:32,042 --> 00:17:33,917
Oh, sorry, yeah. Uh…

229
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,875
- Joe, this is my neighbor Antonella.
- Hi.

230
00:17:35,958 --> 00:17:39,792
Joe and I went to school together
before my parents moved to Staten Island.

231
00:17:39,875 --> 00:17:43,375
Yeah. I actually took, uh, Olivia to prom.

232
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,583
Yes, prom.

233
00:17:46,125 --> 00:17:47,125
Hmm.

234
00:17:48,042 --> 00:17:49,042
Oh.

235
00:17:49,667 --> 00:17:50,667
Yep.

236
00:17:52,250 --> 00:17:53,833
Ah.

237
00:17:53,917 --> 00:17:56,000
It's, um, very nice
to meet you, Antonella.

238
00:17:56,083 --> 00:17:58,625
Well, nice to meet you too. Thank you.

239
00:17:59,292 --> 00:18:01,833
- You don't live on the island, right?
- Oh, no, no, no.

240
00:18:01,917 --> 00:18:06,083
No, when I was a kid, my mom and nonna
would bring me to this market, so…

241
00:18:06,167 --> 00:18:09,167
- I couldn't believe it was still here.
- Yeah, well.

242
00:18:09,833 --> 00:18:13,375
- Great things stand the test of time.
- She's a lawyer.

243
00:18:13,458 --> 00:18:16,167
- No, I'm not.
- A lawyer?

244
00:18:16,250 --> 00:18:19,125
I mean, I'm not yet. I'm...
I went back to school.

245
00:18:19,208 --> 00:18:22,667
I'm in my, uh, first year
JD program at St. John's.

246
00:18:22,750 --> 00:18:24,833
- St. John's, that's impressive.
- Uh…

247
00:18:25,583 --> 00:18:26,583
Yeah.

248
00:18:27,208 --> 00:18:30,167
- Never too late to start all over again.
- Yeah.

249
00:18:31,083 --> 00:18:34,208
- I don't wanna be rude. We're in a rush.
- Of course. Great to see you.

250
00:18:34,292 --> 00:18:36,625
- Thank you.
- You too. Antonella, nice to meet you.

251
00:18:36,708 --> 00:18:39,125
- Thank you. Nice to meet you.
- Thanks, Al.

252
00:18:39,208 --> 00:18:40,667
What's going on?

253
00:18:40,750 --> 00:18:44,292
That's a short but long story.

254
00:18:44,375 --> 00:18:47,000
"Very short but long story."

255
00:18:47,083 --> 00:18:50,292
- I love that phrase. Let's remember that.
- Okay.

256
00:18:50,375 --> 00:18:53,125
Nice, Olivia from high school.
She still hot?

257
00:18:53,208 --> 00:18:54,542
Hot and married.

258
00:18:55,375 --> 00:18:57,333
- Who's still hot?
- I gotta go.

259
00:19:26,500 --> 00:19:29,292
Okay. What are we doing here?
Giving the neighborhood a show?

260
00:19:29,375 --> 00:19:31,000
What? I don't want any tan lines.

261
00:19:31,583 --> 00:19:34,708
Hey, I got something
I wanna tell both of you guys.

262
00:19:34,792 --> 00:19:39,000
I went to, uh, Staten Island
the other day, and I found a restaurant.

263
00:19:40,208 --> 00:19:42,208
What are you doing
going to Staten Island to eat?

264
00:19:42,292 --> 00:19:44,250
Yeah, there's lots
of good restaurants here.

265
00:19:44,333 --> 00:19:47,167
Yeah, I'm not talking
about a restaurant to eat.

266
00:19:47,250 --> 00:19:49,167
I'm talking about a restaurant to buy.

267
00:19:49,875 --> 00:19:50,708
Huh?

268
00:19:50,792 --> 00:19:53,583
- Restaurant to buy?
- Yeah.

269
00:19:53,667 --> 00:19:55,708
- In Staten Island? What?
- Yeah.

270
00:19:55,792 --> 00:19:58,750
What the hell are you talking about?
How'd you buy a restaurant?

271
00:19:58,833 --> 00:20:00,667
With the money my mom left me.

272
00:20:01,917 --> 00:20:03,125
What? Are you crazy?

273
00:20:03,208 --> 00:20:05,667
I don't know. Maybe I am.

274
00:20:05,750 --> 00:20:08,500
But, look, I really do.
I wanna open an Italian restaurant,

275
00:20:08,583 --> 00:20:12,625
and I wanna name it Enoteca Maria.
I wanna name it after my mom.

276
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,292
You don't know the first thing about it.

277
00:20:16,375 --> 00:20:20,333
What is there to know? You make food,
people eat the food, people are happy.

278
00:20:20,417 --> 00:20:25,125
- You told me I need to try something.
- Like buy new furniture, get a girlfriend.

279
00:20:25,208 --> 00:20:26,917
Right, or pay your mortgage,

280
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,958
not start a business
you know nothing about.

281
00:20:29,042 --> 00:20:31,250
Guys, I'm not getting any younger, okay?

282
00:20:31,333 --> 00:20:34,208
And I'm running out of time
to figure this out, all right?

283
00:20:34,292 --> 00:20:35,875
This is what I want.

284
00:20:35,958 --> 00:20:37,792
I dunno how to explain it,

285
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:40,125
but this is what I need.

286
00:20:40,208 --> 00:20:44,333
Listen, I cannot in good conscience
allow you to spend your ma's money

287
00:20:44,417 --> 00:20:46,417
on a restaurant in Staten Island.

288
00:20:47,542 --> 00:20:49,583
I don't think that you understand.

289
00:20:50,292 --> 00:20:51,292
I already did.

290
00:20:54,667 --> 00:20:57,500
Okay, listen, I'm really excited
for you guys to see this place.

291
00:20:57,583 --> 00:21:00,375
It's pretty amazing, okay?
All right. Take a look.

292
00:21:00,458 --> 00:21:02,833
This bar here, I mean,
look how cool that is.

293
00:21:02,917 --> 00:21:05,750
Look at this floor.
This checkerboard, totally authentic.

294
00:21:05,833 --> 00:21:07,917
It's not trying hard,
it just feels terrific.

295
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:12,417
I'm probably gonna take these booths
and clean them out. I don't need them.

296
00:21:13,125 --> 00:21:16,750
- You spent how much on this?
- 175,000 for the down payment.

297
00:21:16,833 --> 00:21:19,000
I mean, I have a mortgage, obviously.

298
00:21:20,667 --> 00:21:24,292
I'm not gonna quit my job at the MTA.
I'll keep it in order to pay the bills.

299
00:21:24,375 --> 00:21:29,458
And I have a solid five months of money
before I even sell one plate of food.

300
00:21:29,542 --> 00:21:30,875
Oh, God!

301
00:21:30,958 --> 00:21:34,875
Okay. Guys, honestly, can you just try?
Just try to keep an open mind.

302
00:21:34,958 --> 00:21:38,958
Because if I don't have you two,
then I don't have anybody, okay?

303
00:21:39,042 --> 00:21:43,333
Now, just walk the place with me
and share my vision. Can you do that?

304
00:21:44,542 --> 00:21:46,917
Okay, this exposed brick right here,

305
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,208
people would literally kill each other
to have that nowadays.

306
00:21:50,292 --> 00:21:54,167
There is a phone booth in the back room
that is just so cool and old-school.

307
00:21:54,250 --> 00:21:58,750
Glance up at those tin-crusted ceilings.
Are you kidding me? That's real.

308
00:21:58,833 --> 00:22:02,833
The way I see this is you would take down
all these walls, maybe put in an archway.

309
00:22:02,917 --> 00:22:05,083
This would be
a beautiful open-air kitchen.

310
00:22:05,167 --> 00:22:09,750
I want the entire place to feel more like
someone's house than a restaurant.

311
00:22:09,833 --> 00:22:13,000
Okay, so, just so I can
wrap my brain around this,

312
00:22:13,083 --> 00:22:14,542
you wanna open a restaurant

313
00:22:14,625 --> 00:22:17,167
with the five dishes you kind of,
sort of know how to make?

314
00:22:17,250 --> 00:22:20,500
No, maybe a dish or two from my family.
But you know what occurred to me?

315
00:22:20,583 --> 00:22:21,708
This is what happened.

316
00:22:21,792 --> 00:22:24,042
I'm going through
my mom's and my nonna's recipes,

317
00:22:24,125 --> 00:22:27,750
and I'm like, "What is going on here?
Why am I searching so hard?"

318
00:22:27,833 --> 00:22:31,875
And then I realized, right,
that food is love.

319
00:22:32,583 --> 00:22:35,667
As long as I have their food,
I'm gonna have them.

320
00:22:35,750 --> 00:22:40,083
I really do want the place to be about
more than just serving someone dinner.

321
00:22:40,167 --> 00:22:43,458
I really, really want this place
to feel like family.

322
00:22:44,583 --> 00:22:48,708
Okay, but Joe, your ma and your nonna,
they're not around.

323
00:22:48,792 --> 00:22:51,958
So, who are you gonna get
to come down and cook like them?

324
00:22:52,750 --> 00:22:55,292
Nonnas.
Other real-life Italian grandmothers.

325
00:22:55,375 --> 00:22:56,625
That's who.

326
00:22:56,708 --> 00:22:59,228
I want 'em to make dishes
that were passed on from their family.

327
00:22:59,292 --> 00:23:01,542
And I wanna share it with everybody.

328
00:23:02,917 --> 00:23:04,250
I love it!

329
00:23:05,250 --> 00:23:06,625
What? I do.

330
00:23:07,125 --> 00:23:08,333
Real-life grandmas!

331
00:23:08,417 --> 00:23:11,333
- Joe, it's a wonderful idea.
- Oh.Thank you.

332
00:23:11,417 --> 00:23:13,792
I mean, who wouldn't want
their grandmothers cooking?

333
00:23:13,875 --> 00:23:17,500
All right, I can...
I can kinda see the appeal, I guess.

334
00:23:17,583 --> 00:23:19,833
Come on, it's a great idea.
You love this idea.

335
00:23:19,917 --> 00:23:21,208
No, I don't love it.

336
00:23:21,292 --> 00:23:22,972
You love it, 'cause if you didn't love it,

337
00:23:23,042 --> 00:23:25,042
you'd have nothing
but a cold, dead heart inside.

338
00:23:25,125 --> 00:23:28,208
Yeah, Bruno.
Stop having a cold, dead heart.

339
00:23:30,125 --> 00:23:32,500
A job like this would take months, okay?

340
00:23:32,583 --> 00:23:36,333
The... The walls, the floor,
the tile, the electric.

341
00:23:36,417 --> 00:23:39,417
Don't get me started on the plumbing
and the ANSUL system, okay?

342
00:23:39,500 --> 00:23:43,292
Who you gonna get to do that work for?
Are you gonna hire a nonna for that?

343
00:23:43,375 --> 00:23:48,417
No, I'm really fortunate, because
my best friend happens to be a contractor.

344
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:52,250
- So I'm fortunate.
- Oh, no. No, no.

345
00:23:52,333 --> 00:23:54,167
- Yes, I am.
- No, no, no!

346
00:23:54,250 --> 00:23:57,500
Not that I'm bringing this up because
I would never, ever bring this up,

347
00:23:57,583 --> 00:24:01,167
but remember I fixed your father's car
out of the goodness of my heart?

348
00:24:01,250 --> 00:24:03,875
- That's bringing it up.
- Only as a source of reference.

349
00:24:03,958 --> 00:24:07,167
You're my best friend. I can fix cars,
and you needed a car fixed.

350
00:24:07,250 --> 00:24:08,958
Cars don't need permits, Joe.

351
00:24:09,042 --> 00:24:12,250
They don't need
building codes, union labor.

352
00:24:12,333 --> 00:24:16,792
You're being impulsive.
You need chefs, a menu, a marketing plan.

353
00:24:16,875 --> 00:24:19,500
You're gonna need
a certificate of occupancy.

354
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:21,500
You're gonna have to pass inspections.

355
00:24:21,583 --> 00:24:23,500
- You're not even listening!
- I'm listening.

356
00:24:23,583 --> 00:24:26,000
I gotta pass inspection
and I need to get menus.

357
00:24:26,083 --> 00:24:28,458
I love you to death.
You are a lot of things,

358
00:24:28,542 --> 00:24:30,833
but a responsible businessman
is not one of 'em.

359
00:24:30,917 --> 00:24:33,042
I know that. That's why I got you.

360
00:24:33,125 --> 00:24:36,667
I promise, I'm gonna pay you back
for all the work you do

361
00:24:36,750 --> 00:24:39,167
the second this place is up and humming.

362
00:24:39,250 --> 00:24:41,583
And I do love to decorate.

363
00:24:41,667 --> 00:24:45,292
I see a wine rack over there
and like a little Benjamin Moore,

364
00:24:45,375 --> 00:24:48,208
splash it up, and maybe
some family photos on the walls.

365
00:24:48,292 --> 00:24:51,292
That's what I'm talking about.
She has a vision for this place already.

366
00:24:51,375 --> 00:24:55,042
- That's exciting!
- You are a crazy son of a saint, you know?

367
00:24:56,750 --> 00:24:58,458
Does that mean you'll do it?

368
00:25:00,542 --> 00:25:03,250
- Yes, I'll do it.
- Come on, this is gonna be fun.

369
00:25:03,333 --> 00:25:05,625
- All right, all right.
- You only live once.

370
00:25:05,708 --> 00:25:09,083
- Don't touch me like that.
- Superman, look at the old phone booth.

371
00:25:15,042 --> 00:25:16,042
Okay.

372
00:25:16,958 --> 00:25:19,333
Joe, where's the bin? I need the bin.

373
00:25:19,417 --> 00:25:22,375
God, I need a paying job. Let's go.

374
00:25:23,500 --> 00:25:25,000
Ay, ay, ay.

375
00:25:26,333 --> 00:25:27,333
What is this?

376
00:25:27,708 --> 00:25:29,208
- A chef?
- Yeah.

377
00:25:30,625 --> 00:25:32,417
Look at me, I can barely move.

378
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:35,333
What are you talking about?
The doctor says you're doing great.

379
00:25:35,417 --> 00:25:37,167
What the hell does he know?

380
00:25:37,250 --> 00:25:41,292
I gotta wear compression socks
to go from here to the bathroom.

381
00:25:41,375 --> 00:25:44,542
I know how unhappy you are
when you're not cooking. It will be great.

382
00:25:44,625 --> 00:25:49,750
- I'm 73 years old. I am done being happy.
- Come on. Age is not a disease, Roberta.

383
00:25:49,833 --> 00:25:52,000
Yeah, well, it's not a cure either.

384
00:25:52,083 --> 00:25:56,292
- Joey, I can't. I can't do this for you.
- I am not asking you to do this for me.

385
00:25:56,375 --> 00:25:59,708
I'm asking you to do it
for you and for mymamma.

386
00:26:03,083 --> 00:26:05,125
- What?
- God rest her soul.

387
00:26:06,667 --> 00:26:09,208
You using Catholic guilt on me?

388
00:26:09,292 --> 00:26:12,458
- I learned it from the best.
- Madone.

389
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:17,083
Look, I'm not saying yes,
but if I did say yes…

390
00:26:17,167 --> 00:26:18,167
Mm-hmm.

391
00:26:18,833 --> 00:26:21,708
…who else would be in the kitchen
cooking with me?

392
00:26:21,792 --> 00:26:24,667
I couldn't feed a restaurant
all by myself.

393
00:26:24,750 --> 00:26:26,500
Trust me, please.

394
00:26:26,583 --> 00:26:27,708
This will be fun.

395
00:26:39,750 --> 00:26:40,750
Hey.

396
00:26:41,375 --> 00:26:42,375
Hey.

397
00:26:43,417 --> 00:26:47,042
All the locals are talking
about, uh, that new restaurant of yours.

398
00:26:47,125 --> 00:26:48,333
Yeah, that's right.

399
00:26:48,417 --> 00:26:51,958
I don't think we've been, uh,
formally introduced. My name is Joe.

400
00:26:52,500 --> 00:26:53,667
I'm Al.

401
00:26:53,750 --> 00:26:58,292
27 Hyatt Street. That was my best friend,
Dominic Spirito's place.

402
00:26:59,042 --> 00:27:05,250
Every baptism, communion,
graduation, birthday, anniversaries…

403
00:27:06,083 --> 00:27:07,708
They were all at Spirito's.

404
00:27:07,792 --> 00:27:11,333
Dominic was there for over 50 years
before he passed away.

405
00:27:11,417 --> 00:27:12,417
Ah.

406
00:27:12,833 --> 00:27:15,000
I'm so sorry for your loss. I didn't know.

407
00:27:16,625 --> 00:27:18,792
You threw his name in the street.

408
00:27:19,708 --> 00:27:23,333
We were working on the building.
I didn't mean any disrespect whatsoever.

409
00:27:24,417 --> 00:27:27,083
I don't trust people
who aren't from around here.

410
00:27:27,583 --> 00:27:30,667
We're not Manhattan,
and we sure as hell ain't no Brooklyn.

411
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:32,875
You're on the island now, pal. You got it?

412
00:27:34,208 --> 00:27:36,333
Yeah, I got it.

413
00:27:39,333 --> 00:27:43,333
Gianni,
what should I tell you about today?

414
00:27:44,542 --> 00:27:51,458
Well, I got up. I made breakfast,
and, um, I took a nap. That was nice.

415
00:27:52,417 --> 00:27:56,125
And then I had lunch,
and now I'm here with you, my darling.

416
00:28:02,208 --> 00:28:03,292
Hello?

417
00:28:03,375 --> 00:28:05,958
Antonella, it's me.

418
00:28:06,042 --> 00:28:08,417
Do we have a doctor's appointment today?

419
00:28:08,500 --> 00:28:12,208
Because if we do, I'm not going
unless it's with the podiatrist.

420
00:28:12,292 --> 00:28:16,500
No, we don't.
But you do have a job interview.

421
00:28:16,583 --> 00:28:17,625
No.

422
00:28:17,708 --> 00:28:19,375
I told you no.

423
00:28:19,458 --> 00:28:22,667
All those old ladies
trying to be chefs, that's ridiculous.

424
00:28:22,750 --> 00:28:24,042
Ridiculous.

425
00:28:25,042 --> 00:28:25,958
It's a sin.

426
00:28:26,042 --> 00:28:27,542
Oh. How is that a sin?

427
00:28:27,625 --> 00:28:31,042
And you told me
that that Joe fellow was astronzo.

428
00:28:31,125 --> 00:28:34,750
I didn't. I said he was an immature jerk
when we were 17. That's all.

429
00:28:35,375 --> 00:28:39,125
All right, you're gonna have to give me
a really good reason why I should go.

430
00:28:40,583 --> 00:28:43,875
Because you sit alone in this house,
and you got more life to live.

431
00:28:45,583 --> 00:28:47,667
- I brought your favorite wrap.
- I'm not going.

432
00:28:53,250 --> 00:28:57,500
I took a water pill about an hour ago.
Your bathroom better be working.

433
00:28:58,167 --> 00:29:02,375
You think I don't have a bathroom?
Oh, look at you with the walking.

434
00:29:03,333 --> 00:29:05,534
Should be a light day.
I mean, everything's ready to go.

435
00:29:06,750 --> 00:29:07,917
Thanks, guys.

436
00:29:11,375 --> 00:29:13,083
Listen, nobody coming.

437
00:29:13,167 --> 00:29:16,875
Everyone will be here in 20 minutes.
Sit and relax. You're doing so good.

438
00:29:19,750 --> 00:29:23,125
- This list of Craig.
- No, it's Craigslist.

439
00:29:23,917 --> 00:29:25,833
This Craig, is he reliable?

440
00:29:25,917 --> 00:29:28,750
No, no, it's not a he, okay? It's an it.

441
00:29:28,833 --> 00:29:31,333
It's a place where people kinda, you know,

442
00:29:31,417 --> 00:29:34,042
post things they're selling
or like job descriptions.

443
00:29:34,125 --> 00:29:35,250
Like the newspaper.

444
00:29:35,333 --> 00:29:37,917
Yes, except it's online, right?

445
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:41,292
It's online, so anyone can go on
from anywhere and look at it.

446
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:45,458
- You should've put it in the papers.
- Uh… okay.

447
00:29:49,417 --> 00:29:52,667
Roberta, do you know how my nonna
made her Sunday gravy?

448
00:29:52,750 --> 00:29:55,250
There was always
this kind of sweet aftertaste.

449
00:29:55,333 --> 00:29:58,583
Do you know the exact ingredients
that she would put into it?

450
00:29:58,667 --> 00:30:02,958
Joey, that's like asking a woman
to show you hermundate.

451
00:30:03,042 --> 00:30:05,917
Mundate? I don't even...
What kind of guy do you think I am?

452
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:09,000
- I don't even... What is amundate?
- Better not ask.

453
00:30:09,083 --> 00:30:11,667
I'm sorry. I wouldn't ask
to see anyone'smundate,

454
00:30:11,750 --> 00:30:13,875
but I've been kind of kicking myself,

455
00:30:13,958 --> 00:30:16,792
I never had them
write any of this stuff down.

456
00:30:16,875 --> 00:30:19,250
I don't know exactly,
and if I knew exactly,

457
00:30:19,333 --> 00:30:22,000
it wouldn't have been
your nonna's gravy, would it?

458
00:30:23,667 --> 00:30:26,542
It's the secret that makes it special.

459
00:30:28,333 --> 00:30:31,583
Try sugar.
You need a lot more than you think.

460
00:30:31,667 --> 00:30:35,375
- I put a ton of sugar in it.
- Well, there are different kinds.

461
00:30:35,875 --> 00:30:39,375
You get the savory
when you find the sweet.

462
00:30:39,958 --> 00:30:44,792
Okay, listen,
I made this entire scarf sitting here.

463
00:30:44,875 --> 00:30:46,083
I hope you like it.

464
00:30:47,292 --> 00:30:49,333
- For you.
- It's so nice. Thank you.

465
00:30:49,417 --> 00:30:51,125
- You're welcome. Enjoy.
- Thank you.

466
00:30:51,208 --> 00:30:53,292
- It's nice and warm for you.
- Super beautiful.

467
00:30:53,375 --> 00:30:56,500
Okay, I'm calling the shuttle.
I got poker at 3:00.

468
00:30:56,583 --> 00:30:59,458
No, no, no. Give me 20 minutes.
Listen to me. Will you stop?

469
00:30:59,542 --> 00:31:01,208
- I gave you three hours.
- No.

470
00:31:01,292 --> 00:31:04,667
I watched you move boxes.
See you move bottles.

471
00:31:04,750 --> 00:31:07,417
Now, what's gonna happen,
is the other people are gonna join us…

472
00:31:07,500 --> 00:31:09,042
- Nobody's coming!
- They're coming.

473
00:31:09,125 --> 00:31:11,417
- Don't go. 45 minutes...
- I'm sick of watching you...

474
00:31:11,500 --> 00:31:14,708
Look at this. You made it.
Isn't that great? Everyone made it.

475
00:31:14,792 --> 00:31:15,833
This is great!

476
00:31:15,917 --> 00:31:18,667
Calm yourself. She forced me.

477
00:31:18,750 --> 00:31:20,708
Sometimes she needs
a little push out the door.

478
00:31:20,792 --> 00:31:21,958
She literally pushed me.

479
00:31:22,042 --> 00:31:26,250
- Here you go. Looks great. Your stuff.
- All right, I'm here.

480
00:31:26,333 --> 00:31:28,792
- I got class. I'll come pick you up.
- What do you mean?

481
00:31:28,875 --> 00:31:30,208
You have fun.

482
00:31:30,292 --> 00:31:31,125
Huh?

483
00:31:31,208 --> 00:31:32,208
Have fun.

484
00:31:32,250 --> 00:31:34,750
Hey, thank you so much
for bringing her. I appreciate it.

485
00:31:34,833 --> 00:31:36,750
Of course.
I'd do anything in the world for her.

486
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:39,000
By the way,

487
00:31:39,750 --> 00:31:42,500
it's a really great idea. I hope it works.

488
00:31:43,250 --> 00:31:44,250
Thanks.

489
00:31:44,958 --> 00:31:45,792
All right.

490
00:31:45,875 --> 00:31:50,792
Well, Antonella, this is Roberta
and she is a chef at Enoteca Maria.

491
00:31:50,875 --> 00:31:51,875
Se.

492
00:31:53,500 --> 00:31:54,500
Se?

493
00:31:55,958 --> 00:31:57,792
So you're Sicilian?

494
00:31:57,875 --> 00:31:59,542
Se.I'm from Sicily.

495
00:32:01,625 --> 00:32:04,292
- And where are you from?
- I am from Bologna.

496
00:32:05,125 --> 00:32:06,917
- Bologna.
- Sì.

497
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:08,000
Hmm.

498
00:32:08,083 --> 00:32:09,958
I spit on Bologna!

499
00:32:10,042 --> 00:32:11,500
- Is that so?
- Se!

500
00:32:12,708 --> 00:32:15,000
Well, I spit on Sicily, okay?

501
00:32:15,083 --> 00:32:16,417
Don't you spit on Sicily!

502
00:32:16,500 --> 00:32:19,208
This is great!
This is like music to my ears.

503
00:32:19,292 --> 00:32:21,125
Ah, no, no, no! Passion's good.

504
00:32:21,208 --> 00:32:24,083
- You got thegrande bocca!
- You are a put tan a.

505
00:32:24,167 --> 00:32:26,958
- Oh, hi. How are you?
- What? What do you want?

506
00:32:27,042 --> 00:32:28,708
I think I have the wrong address.

507
00:32:28,792 --> 00:32:33,292
No, no, you're at the exact right place.
I'm so sorry. Are you here to be a chef?

508
00:32:33,375 --> 00:32:35,375
- Yes.
- Don't say that! Not nice!

509
00:32:35,458 --> 00:32:36,750
Excellent. What is your name?

510
00:32:36,833 --> 00:32:38,250
- Didn't say that.
- Teresa.

511
00:32:38,333 --> 00:32:42,083
Teresa. What a beautiful name.
May I invite you to join the other ladies?

512
00:32:42,167 --> 00:32:45,000
- I never met anybody like you.
- Get lost, you old bag!

513
00:32:45,083 --> 00:32:49,542
Teresa, will you come join Antonella.
She's from Bologna, she is from Sicily.

514
00:32:49,625 --> 00:32:51,125
- This is Roberta.
- Hello.

515
00:32:51,208 --> 00:32:52,917
- And where are you from?
- Uh…

516
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:56,417
- Well, actually, I'm from the Bronx.
- Great.

517
00:32:58,042 --> 00:33:02,083
Just have fun and cook like you're cooking
for your own family, all right?

518
00:33:02,167 --> 00:33:03,417
The kitchen is yours.

519
00:33:15,458 --> 00:33:16,458
What?

520
00:33:28,125 --> 00:33:30,458
- You need some garlic?
- No!

521
00:33:45,042 --> 00:33:48,250
Lazy Mary, you better get up
She answered back I am not able…

522
00:33:48,333 --> 00:33:49,958
Stop. Stop.

523
00:33:50,042 --> 00:33:51,083
No, no.

524
00:33:52,125 --> 00:33:53,000
There.

525
00:33:53,083 --> 00:33:57,792
Lazy Mary you better get up
We need the sheets for the table

526
00:33:58,792 --> 00:34:04,625
Lazy Mary you smoke in bed
There's only one man you should marry

527
00:34:05,875 --> 00:34:10,125
My advice to you would be
Is to pay attention to me

528
00:34:30,958 --> 00:34:32,500
Hmm!

529
00:34:33,208 --> 00:34:34,208
Oh, my God.

530
00:34:34,667 --> 00:34:39,917
This cheese is perfectly crisp and yet
stays so gooey on your pizza, incredible.

531
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:41,083
Grazie.

532
00:34:41,167 --> 00:34:45,583
Roberta, I mean, that oxtail stew
just melts right in your mouth.

533
00:34:45,667 --> 00:34:46,667
Yeah.

534
00:34:46,750 --> 00:34:47,958
So beautiful.

535
00:34:50,125 --> 00:34:52,208
I'm not talking to you.

536
00:34:52,292 --> 00:34:53,625
I'm not even talking to you.

537
00:34:53,708 --> 00:34:56,542
Where did you come from?
Did you fall out of the sky somewhere?

538
00:34:56,625 --> 00:35:00,042
You have that beautifully seasoned garlic,
but it's right inside the steak.

539
00:35:00,125 --> 00:35:01,708
Where did you learn to do that?

540
00:35:02,917 --> 00:35:04,458
At the convent.

541
00:35:05,917 --> 00:35:08,292
Convent? Are you a nun?

542
00:35:09,125 --> 00:35:11,917
- And you with that language.
- A blessed calling.

543
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:14,917
- Yes, sure.
- Well, I'm a retired nun.

544
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:19,917
I served for many years
at the CFR convent in the Bronx.

545
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:21,000
- Oh.
- Oh.

546
00:35:21,500 --> 00:35:23,958
If it's okay to ask, why'd you leave?

547
00:35:26,125 --> 00:35:29,792
Well, I loved my devotion. I just thought
it was time for something new.

548
00:35:29,875 --> 00:35:33,250
And a friend's son
saw your ad in the list.

549
00:35:33,333 --> 00:35:34,750
Craig, the bum.

550
00:35:35,333 --> 00:35:36,500
Stop.

551
00:35:36,583 --> 00:35:40,750
And I felt God was speaking to me,
telling me to come.

552
00:35:42,125 --> 00:35:44,542
Giving me a… another chance.

553
00:35:48,625 --> 00:35:52,042
So, Joe, who's got the job?

554
00:35:54,792 --> 00:35:55,792
All of you guys.

555
00:35:55,875 --> 00:35:57,583
- This is incredible.
- Oh!

556
00:35:57,667 --> 00:35:59,875
We got a Murderers' Row here.
Look at this.

557
00:35:59,958 --> 00:36:02,792
Are you kidding me?
I wish we could open the doors today.

558
00:36:07,917 --> 00:36:09,750
Cheers, salute.

559
00:36:12,167 --> 00:36:13,750
I'm so grateful.

560
00:36:28,125 --> 00:36:32,375
Look, I've given you a ton of leeway,
and you keep showing up late.

561
00:36:32,458 --> 00:36:35,917
Okay? So I can't do it anymore.
This is your last warning.

562
00:36:37,667 --> 00:36:38,708
Okay.

563
00:36:38,792 --> 00:36:40,125
Uh oh!

564
00:36:40,208 --> 00:36:43,208
Oh, there he is. Dead man walking.

565
00:36:43,292 --> 00:36:45,250
Got called at the principal's office.

566
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:47,708
I gotta ask you guys a favor.

567
00:36:47,792 --> 00:36:50,042
- Yeah, sure.
- Whatever you need.

568
00:36:50,125 --> 00:36:53,375
I just got written up again,
and I cannot lose this job.

569
00:36:53,458 --> 00:36:58,042
So, do you mind covering for me with Dan?
Because I'm gonna be late to work a lot.

570
00:36:58,625 --> 00:37:00,417
Why, Joey? What's going on?

571
00:37:01,958 --> 00:37:03,000
Can you keep a secret?

572
00:37:14,375 --> 00:37:15,583
Fourteen…

573
00:37:29,042 --> 00:37:30,042
Let's see.

574
00:37:32,375 --> 00:37:33,875
- Ah, no.
- Well, I had to.

575
00:37:33,958 --> 00:37:36,167
Refinance your ma's home. What's next?

576
00:37:36,250 --> 00:37:39,167
Next is Enoteca Maria has to work
because there's no other option.

577
00:37:39,250 --> 00:37:42,292
You got me in a difficult position.
I'm one of the people you owe money to.

578
00:37:42,375 --> 00:37:45,458
I know, but you're also my friend.
I need someone to talk to. Complicated.

579
00:37:45,542 --> 00:37:49,750
I need you to think this through.
If you get out now, you could break even.

580
00:37:49,833 --> 00:37:53,083
But if you stay in and it fails,
you could lose everything.

581
00:37:53,167 --> 00:37:57,167
Bruno, I have this feeling deep in my gut
that this whole thing is gonna pay off.

582
00:37:57,708 --> 00:38:00,083
You're my best friend,
so you stay, I stay.

583
00:38:00,167 --> 00:38:04,542
I appreciate it. We got great chefs.
We got food from all over Italy.

584
00:38:04,625 --> 00:38:08,583
- Gotta make sure you get good desserts.
- Yeah. We just passed that place.

585
00:38:08,667 --> 00:38:11,208
I'm getting stressed with the talking.
I'm gonna crush a sub.

586
00:38:11,292 --> 00:38:13,875
- I could do a cutlet.
- You wanna do a cutlet? Come do a cutlet.

587
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:17,333
Here's what I'm thinking. We can always
get desserts that are homemade.

588
00:38:17,417 --> 00:38:18,292
What?

589
00:38:18,375 --> 00:38:20,500
Just hear me out on this, okay?

590
00:38:20,583 --> 00:38:23,375
You're a terrific baker.
The stuff you make is incredible.

591
00:38:23,458 --> 00:38:26,750
It brought my mom so much joy.
I'm just asking you to share that.

592
00:38:26,833 --> 00:38:28,958
I bake for fun. I don't bake serious.

593
00:38:29,042 --> 00:38:33,042
This should be fun. Do something that's
fun for you and fun with everybody else.

594
00:38:33,125 --> 00:38:37,375
- I like doing hair. That's my job.
- You have a job, and you're good at it.

595
00:38:37,458 --> 00:38:41,083
But you have other gifts. This is a chance
to do something that you love.

596
00:38:41,167 --> 00:38:45,958
Sweetie, it sounds exciting,
but I… I really can't. I'm sorry.

597
00:38:46,042 --> 00:38:48,875
I can't even hear that.
I know this is the right thing.

598
00:38:48,958 --> 00:38:51,750
- Is begging gonna help?
- Oh. Damn it.

599
00:38:51,833 --> 00:38:55,625
- Are you okay?
- Damn it, damn it. My hands are going.

600
00:38:55,708 --> 00:38:59,167
Some days are worse. I don't know
how much longer I'll be able to do this.

601
00:38:59,250 --> 00:39:01,518
I'm so sorry. I didn't know
your hands were bothering you.

602
00:39:01,542 --> 00:39:03,667
Is that something ongoing?
Sorry you're in that.

603
00:39:03,750 --> 00:39:05,583
Don't be sad for me. Do not be sad for me.

604
00:39:05,667 --> 00:39:07,750
I've led a great life
exactly how I wanted to,

605
00:39:07,833 --> 00:39:10,833
and you know the stories,
and I have no regrets.

606
00:39:10,917 --> 00:39:11,917
And, uh…

607
00:39:13,083 --> 00:39:14,500
I am okay.

608
00:39:14,583 --> 00:39:17,833
Yeah, well, you deserve
to be better than okay.

609
00:39:18,708 --> 00:39:19,708
You deserve to be great.

610
00:39:19,792 --> 00:39:22,625
We only have so much time,
so let me just accept this yes.

611
00:39:22,708 --> 00:39:25,934
I'll see you tomorrow at the restaurant.
Don't let me down. Love you and thank you.

612
00:39:25,958 --> 00:39:29,875
You are so manipulative.
Don't hold your breath.

613
00:39:29,958 --> 00:39:31,917
Appreciate your patience. Love the color.

614
00:39:34,333 --> 00:39:38,333
Gia, who wants to start over at this age?

615
00:39:43,542 --> 00:39:47,125
This is my main dish on the menu.

616
00:39:48,208 --> 00:39:49,917
What is that? It stinks.

617
00:39:50,708 --> 00:39:52,833
Capuzzelle.

618
00:39:52,917 --> 00:39:54,292
Dear God, save us.

619
00:39:54,792 --> 00:39:58,083
- That is definitely a bold choice.
- How are you gonna put that on a menu?

620
00:39:58,167 --> 00:39:59,250
Are you crazy?

621
00:39:59,333 --> 00:40:02,500
Capuzzelleis from my family village.

622
00:40:02,583 --> 00:40:05,458
Capuzzelleis my identity.

623
00:40:05,542 --> 00:40:08,333
Well, change your identity.

624
00:40:10,250 --> 00:40:13,708
Hey, wow, I'm so glad you made it.

625
00:40:14,542 --> 00:40:15,542
I'm here.

626
00:40:16,167 --> 00:40:18,625
This is Gia. She's our pastry chef.

627
00:40:18,708 --> 00:40:21,542
- And you know Roberta, obviously.
- Oh yeah.

628
00:40:22,250 --> 00:40:26,000
- This is Teresa and, uh, Antonella.
- Hello.

629
00:40:26,083 --> 00:40:27,083
Ladies.

630
00:40:29,708 --> 00:40:31,917
- Apron?
- Please. They're right over here.

631
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:36,500
Thank you.

632
00:40:36,583 --> 00:40:39,000
Pa-pa-pa-pa. They bounce.

633
00:40:47,417 --> 00:40:50,375
Hey, I… it's an apron,
not an evening gown.

634
00:40:50,458 --> 00:40:55,708
Well, every opportunity
is an opportunity to look good.

635
00:40:55,792 --> 00:40:58,208
How do you bake over those things?

636
00:40:59,708 --> 00:41:00,958
Years of practice.

637
00:41:02,208 --> 00:41:03,500
Wow.

638
00:41:03,583 --> 00:41:05,875
- Okay, where were we?
- Mi capuzzelle.

639
00:41:05,958 --> 00:41:08,625
Oh, that's what smells.
I thought maybe it was me.

640
00:41:08,708 --> 00:41:09,583
Oh, God.

641
00:41:09,667 --> 00:41:12,208
Wasn't sure.

642
00:41:12,292 --> 00:41:14,625
- No.
- What iscapuzzelle?

643
00:41:17,125 --> 00:41:18,833
Okay, so it's a simple story.

644
00:41:18,917 --> 00:41:22,042
My mother came from a village
that was very, very poor.

645
00:41:22,125 --> 00:41:24,583
So they had to use the entire animal.

646
00:41:24,667 --> 00:41:28,500
So, you stuff the head
with some crumbs of bread.

647
00:41:28,583 --> 00:41:30,292
Breadcrumbs.

648
00:41:31,750 --> 00:41:33,333
Mi scusi.

649
00:41:33,417 --> 00:41:35,542
- Breadcrumbs.
- Hmm.

650
00:41:36,167 --> 00:41:38,500
A little of this, a little of that.

651
00:41:38,583 --> 00:41:40,833
In the oven, thecapuzzelle.

652
00:41:42,792 --> 00:41:44,250
Bye-bye, baby.

653
00:41:46,542 --> 00:41:49,708
All right, the sheep's head is in.
Now, let's move on to sauce.

654
00:41:49,792 --> 00:41:52,542
Oh, oh, oh, my mother's sauce.

655
00:41:52,625 --> 00:41:55,167
Yes, of course, your mother's sauce,
or your nonna's sauce,

656
00:41:55,250 --> 00:41:58,750
or your Great Aunt Mary's sauce,
as long as it is your family's sauce.

657
00:41:58,833 --> 00:41:59,833
Thanks.

658
00:41:59,917 --> 00:42:01,667
- We'll do cannolis for dessert.
- Great.

659
00:42:01,750 --> 00:42:02,750
Perfect.

660
00:42:11,125 --> 00:42:14,125
Gia, can you do me a favor?
Do you mind tasting all of these?

661
00:42:14,208 --> 00:42:17,292
Tell me which one you think
should be on the menu? You be the judge.

662
00:42:17,375 --> 00:42:22,083
Oh, sure. Well, if they taste
half as good as they smell,

663
00:42:22,167 --> 00:42:23,500
this is gonna be difficult.

664
00:42:23,583 --> 00:42:26,167
- Yeah, but just be honest.
- Okay.

665
00:42:49,833 --> 00:42:51,708
- Is this your nonna's?
- No.

666
00:42:51,792 --> 00:42:54,500
I mean, I tried maple syrup, brown sugar.

667
00:42:54,583 --> 00:42:55,667
I tried honey.

668
00:42:55,750 --> 00:43:00,333
There's just no combination I do
that makes it taste like my nonna's gravy.

669
00:43:00,417 --> 00:43:02,667
- Well, you keep trying.
- Yeah.

670
00:43:10,292 --> 00:43:12,042
Hmm. Is that almonds in there?

671
00:43:12,125 --> 00:43:14,500
Sì, pesto alla trapanese.

672
00:43:14,583 --> 00:43:16,042
From Sicily.

673
00:43:16,125 --> 00:43:17,125
Bah!

674
00:43:18,542 --> 00:43:21,917
They're all so good. I don't know
how you're gonna choose. They're perfect.

675
00:43:22,000 --> 00:43:25,958
Joe, we could rotate the sauces
week to week.

676
00:43:26,042 --> 00:43:27,875
- That's a great idea.
- Fabulous.

677
00:43:27,958 --> 00:43:30,417
That's exactly what we'll do.
Let's taste what you were doing.

678
00:43:33,125 --> 00:43:36,208
- Pesto alla trapanese, huh?
- Sì.

679
00:43:36,292 --> 00:43:39,125
My people created Parmigiano Reggiano.

680
00:43:39,208 --> 00:43:41,125
That's something to boast about!

681
00:43:41,208 --> 00:43:43,625
- Parmigiano Reggiano.
- That's right.

682
00:43:43,708 --> 00:43:45,833
My people created the cannoli!

683
00:43:45,917 --> 00:43:48,667
- Cannoli? Are you crazy? It's nothing.
- Yes!

684
00:43:48,750 --> 00:43:51,542
- What do you mean nothing?
- Stuffed cream for Christ's sake.

685
00:43:51,625 --> 00:43:52,985
- What do you know?
- Get outta here.

686
00:43:53,042 --> 00:43:55,917
You think you know everything
'cause you're from Bologna!

687
00:43:56,000 --> 00:43:59,375
- Listen to this.
- Your people are mean and ugly and cold.

688
00:43:59,458 --> 00:44:01,833
Your people are crude and vulgar.

689
00:44:01,917 --> 00:44:03,750
- Okay, okay, okay.
- Puttana.

690
00:44:03,833 --> 00:44:07,750
And don't you spit any more at me
'cause you're gonna pay a debt for that.

691
00:44:07,833 --> 00:44:11,208
Let me tell you right now,
you make something outta this.

692
00:44:14,042 --> 00:44:16,042
You… What?

693
00:44:16,125 --> 00:44:18,042
- Uh-huh. Yeah.
- You wanna fight?

694
00:44:18,125 --> 00:44:19,167
Yeah.

695
00:44:20,542 --> 00:44:21,792
How's this?

696
00:44:21,875 --> 00:44:25,083
I'm going to throw something at you,
you beast.

697
00:44:25,167 --> 00:44:27,250
What? How dare you?

698
00:44:27,333 --> 00:44:29,250
- Oh, see if…
- How dare you?

699
00:44:29,333 --> 00:44:31,625
I'm worried. I'm scared of you.

700
00:44:32,542 --> 00:44:34,667
All right, go ahead. Go get it!

701
00:44:36,083 --> 00:44:38,625
They could hurt themselves, Joe.
You've gotta stop this.

702
00:44:38,708 --> 00:44:41,125
- No, let them fight it out.
- It's the Italian way.

703
00:44:41,208 --> 00:44:42,667
Have a little arugula!

704
00:44:42,750 --> 00:44:45,042
- Madre di Dio.
- Why don't you? Go ahead.

705
00:44:45,125 --> 00:44:48,250
- Puttana! How dare you?
- Ow! Oh!

706
00:44:49,833 --> 00:44:51,083
Ow!

707
00:44:51,167 --> 00:44:52,625
I'm going to get you.

708
00:44:57,667 --> 00:44:59,250
Mi capuzzelle!

709
00:45:07,208 --> 00:45:12,917
This is a violation
for fire code defiance.

710
00:45:13,000 --> 00:45:16,292
Your ANSUL system was shut off.
You're lucky no one got hurt.

711
00:45:16,375 --> 00:45:18,458
Yeah. Oh, I'm sorry.

712
00:45:20,375 --> 00:45:22,958
Oh my God. Look at that.
I'm already supposed to be somewhere.

713
00:45:23,042 --> 00:45:25,726
So if we're all wrapped up,
if you don't mind, I'd love to get going.

714
00:45:25,750 --> 00:45:30,000
Oh! Of course. You know,
I don't wanna hold up your day.

715
00:45:30,083 --> 00:45:31,500
Okay, thank you so much.

716
00:45:33,083 --> 00:45:35,625
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry too, Joey.

717
00:45:35,708 --> 00:45:37,000
It was her fault.

718
00:45:37,083 --> 00:45:38,083
It's her fault.

719
00:45:38,167 --> 00:45:40,083
You are killing me.
I still believe in you.

720
00:45:40,167 --> 00:45:44,250
Maybe one good idea we can take from this
is not to fight in the kitchen, okay?

721
00:45:44,333 --> 00:45:47,167
So sorry. I'm late for work.
I gotta run. Bye. Love you guys.

722
00:45:52,542 --> 00:45:55,875
Can't you two just offer
to forgive each other?

723
00:45:58,125 --> 00:46:00,500
To forgive is divine.

724
00:46:03,000 --> 00:46:04,750
Oh, she started it.

725
00:46:07,292 --> 00:46:10,583
Hey, Vito, Joe punched in.
Have you seen Joe?

726
00:46:10,667 --> 00:46:12,250
How you doing, Mr. McClane?

727
00:46:12,333 --> 00:46:15,792
He was here like, two hours ago?
Yeah, two hours ago.

728
00:46:15,875 --> 00:46:19,417
I think he's over in maintenance
with Luis in North Garage.

729
00:46:19,500 --> 00:46:20,875
Okay, thanks.

730
00:46:27,000 --> 00:46:28,875
Hey, Luis, where's Joe?

731
00:46:35,542 --> 00:46:36,917
Right, thank you.

732
00:46:38,583 --> 00:46:39,833
I called you a putz.

733
00:46:42,167 --> 00:46:44,250
Omar, where's Joe?

734
00:46:44,333 --> 00:46:47,292
I'm not sure.
He was helping me mount some tires.

735
00:46:47,375 --> 00:46:50,500
My guess is he's back
at the main depot with Vito now.

736
00:46:50,583 --> 00:46:52,125
- You're kidding me!
- Yeah.

737
00:46:55,875 --> 00:46:59,000
Vito, where the hell is Joe?

738
00:46:59,083 --> 00:47:01,958
Mr. McClane, where you been all day?

739
00:47:03,250 --> 00:47:05,083
That's lunch!

740
00:47:24,083 --> 00:47:25,292
- Wow.
- Hey.

741
00:47:25,375 --> 00:47:27,292
I love what you've done with the place.

742
00:47:27,375 --> 00:47:30,250
- Yeah. You like it?
- You're crushing it.

743
00:47:30,333 --> 00:47:33,292
I was thinking,
should I do that room and set that on fire

744
00:47:33,375 --> 00:47:34,958
and just connect the two places?

745
00:47:35,042 --> 00:47:36,167
- Too much.
- Yeah?

746
00:47:38,208 --> 00:47:39,500
Antonella sent me.

747
00:47:39,583 --> 00:47:42,417
She wants you to have
this card from the dollar store.

748
00:47:42,500 --> 00:47:45,167
And I think there might be $20 in that.

749
00:47:45,250 --> 00:47:47,708
- Very nice. Look at that.
- Yeah.

750
00:47:47,792 --> 00:47:51,125
Roberta gave me $10, so I'm actually
gonna come out ahead in this one.

751
00:47:51,208 --> 00:47:52,375
Yeah, wow. Lucky you.

752
00:47:52,458 --> 00:47:54,833
A little Italian lightning
struck the place.

753
00:47:58,250 --> 00:47:59,542
I wanna help clean.

754
00:48:01,083 --> 00:48:02,583
Where's your trash bags?

755
00:48:02,667 --> 00:48:04,792
Oh, um, just underneath there.

756
00:48:04,875 --> 00:48:05,875
Okay.

757
00:48:06,250 --> 00:48:07,292
Thanks.

758
00:48:07,375 --> 00:48:09,792
No, really? That's crazy.

759
00:48:09,875 --> 00:48:11,583
So, what was she taking?

760
00:48:11,667 --> 00:48:12,542
Butter.

761
00:48:12,625 --> 00:48:16,042
No, I'm serious.
The plastic square butters from the diner.

762
00:48:16,125 --> 00:48:18,542
Trust me,
I know exactly what you're talking about.

763
00:48:18,625 --> 00:48:21,667
My mom used to do the exact same thing.

764
00:48:21,750 --> 00:48:25,167
Yeah, well, Antonella's fridge?
Filled with them.

765
00:48:25,250 --> 00:48:28,208
I asked her, like,
how much butter does one person need?

766
00:48:28,292 --> 00:48:31,000
How long have you and, uh,
Antonella been neighbors?

767
00:48:31,083 --> 00:48:32,625
Oh, God, what?

768
00:48:32,708 --> 00:48:37,167
My husband and I bought
the house next door… eight years ago?

769
00:48:37,250 --> 00:48:40,000
And then it was a fixer-upper,
so we renovated.

770
00:48:40,083 --> 00:48:43,833
And she complained
about the noise every day.

771
00:48:44,917 --> 00:48:48,167
Well, you must've gotten past it,
'cause you two seem very close.

772
00:48:48,750 --> 00:48:49,625
Yeah.

773
00:48:49,708 --> 00:48:51,417
Yeah, she, um…

774
00:48:53,292 --> 00:48:56,958
After my husband passed away,
she was amazing.

775
00:48:57,958 --> 00:48:59,625
She wouldn't leave me alone.

776
00:48:59,708 --> 00:49:02,083
She would come over and sit with me,

777
00:49:03,375 --> 00:49:04,917
and cook for me,

778
00:49:05,708 --> 00:49:07,250
and make me take a shower.

779
00:49:09,667 --> 00:49:11,917
It's a special kind of love, you know?

780
00:49:14,958 --> 00:49:18,833
Olivia, I am so sorry to hear that.
I had no idea.

781
00:49:18,917 --> 00:49:21,500
Oh, come on, stop. How would you know?

782
00:49:22,458 --> 00:49:26,333
She keeps telling me I should move
my wedding ring to the other hand, but…

783
00:49:28,125 --> 00:49:30,042
I don't know. I just don't feel ready.

784
00:49:30,625 --> 00:49:31,458
You know?

785
00:49:31,542 --> 00:49:33,958
Yeah. Trust me, I understand.

786
00:49:34,667 --> 00:49:35,958
Yeah?

787
00:49:38,833 --> 00:49:42,792
My mom left me
this letter, but I haven't opened it yet,

788
00:49:42,875 --> 00:49:45,708
because I feel like once I do open it,

789
00:49:45,792 --> 00:49:49,125
that'll be the last thing
she ever says to me, you know, so…

790
00:49:50,083 --> 00:49:51,458
Joe…

791
00:49:52,875 --> 00:49:53,875
I'm sorry.

792
00:49:55,833 --> 00:49:57,125
It just hurts.

793
00:50:00,458 --> 00:50:01,667
Grief.

794
00:50:01,750 --> 00:50:05,333
It doesn't have a timeline,
so why should we?

795
00:50:10,708 --> 00:50:11,708
Yeah.

796
00:50:32,708 --> 00:50:33,708
Hey.

797
00:50:34,375 --> 00:50:35,708
Sturdy, isn't she?

798
00:50:36,958 --> 00:50:39,042
Completely gutted.
Built from the ground up.

799
00:50:39,125 --> 00:50:41,750
Every piece of wood, every piling.

800
00:50:41,833 --> 00:50:43,500
- Yeah.
- Top-notch.

801
00:50:43,583 --> 00:50:46,083
Okay, um… You're the owner?

802
00:50:46,167 --> 00:50:47,375
Yeah. Yes.

803
00:50:47,458 --> 00:50:49,000
You failed. Twice.

804
00:50:49,083 --> 00:50:50,083
What?

805
00:50:50,958 --> 00:50:52,542
Yeah, um, first of all,

806
00:50:53,208 --> 00:50:57,875
there was a kitchen fire that's affecting
the integrity and safety of that wall.

807
00:50:57,958 --> 00:50:59,917
No. That's impossible. There's no fire.

808
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:03,167
There was a… little bit of a problem
with a sheep's head, but…

809
00:51:03,250 --> 00:51:04,417
A what?

810
00:51:04,500 --> 00:51:06,875
And number two, you need a new oven

811
00:51:07,583 --> 00:51:11,792
because you got remnants
of carbon dioxide and nitrogen in there.

812
00:51:11,875 --> 00:51:14,958
That's easy. I can run out
and grab the new oven right now.

813
00:51:15,042 --> 00:51:18,458
- We can take care of that off the list.
- It's a custom-made specialty oven.

814
00:51:18,542 --> 00:51:21,792
You can't just pull up to a store
and have them throw it in your trunk.

815
00:51:21,875 --> 00:51:26,875
On the bright side, your sprinkler system
is working fine, so, you know…

816
00:51:28,667 --> 00:51:29,667
Have a good day.

817
00:51:29,708 --> 00:51:31,125
I'm so sorry.

818
00:51:31,208 --> 00:51:34,708
Would it be possible to do anything else
we could do to keep this moving?

819
00:51:34,792 --> 00:51:39,083
- I really need to get these doors open.
- You can reapply for inspection.

820
00:51:39,167 --> 00:51:42,208
Great. And what are we talking about?
What works for your schedule?

821
00:51:42,292 --> 00:51:44,250
Would that be later
this week or next week?

822
00:51:45,542 --> 00:51:46,542
Oh, sorry.

823
00:51:47,583 --> 00:51:49,708
I like this guy. "Next week."

824
00:51:49,792 --> 00:51:54,250
Um… Try "next year."
The waiting list is a mile long, pal.

825
00:51:54,917 --> 00:51:57,542
You're not opening any time soon, man.

826
00:51:58,750 --> 00:52:00,042
If ever.

827
00:52:06,750 --> 00:52:08,875
There was a sheep's head fire?

828
00:52:10,083 --> 00:52:11,833
What the hell does that even mean?

829
00:52:12,708 --> 00:52:15,833
- Roberta with hercapuzzelle.
- Why didn't you tell me?

830
00:52:17,208 --> 00:52:19,125
I… Honestly, I didn't think it was…

831
00:52:19,208 --> 00:52:22,125
I didn't think it'd matter.
It was just a fire. I cleaned it up...

832
00:52:22,208 --> 00:52:23,958
Joe, a sheep's head catches fire

833
00:52:24,042 --> 00:52:26,417
compromising the integrity
of the walls I built?

834
00:52:26,500 --> 00:52:28,917
- Right.
- Don't think it's important to tell me?

835
00:52:29,833 --> 00:52:32,500
Okay. Bruno. Let's just calm down.

836
00:52:32,583 --> 00:52:34,542
- Everyone's upset. I'm upset.
- I am calm.

837
00:52:34,625 --> 00:52:35,917
- Okay. Good.
- Okay?

838
00:52:36,542 --> 00:52:37,958
- But listen to me.
- I'm listening.

839
00:52:38,042 --> 00:52:40,625
If you fail an inspection, that's it.

840
00:52:41,167 --> 00:52:43,333
You have no certificate of occupancy.

841
00:52:43,417 --> 00:52:46,542
You can't run a restaurant
if you don't have a building.

842
00:52:47,167 --> 00:52:50,542
I'll find another way.
I'll find another way to keep it going.

843
00:52:50,625 --> 00:52:53,458
With what money?
You don't have any money left!

844
00:52:53,542 --> 00:52:55,583
I could take out a loan
against my pension.

845
00:52:55,667 --> 00:52:57,250
Joe, listen to yourself.

846
00:52:57,333 --> 00:52:59,213
I got credit cards.
I can take out credit cards.

847
00:52:59,292 --> 00:53:02,792
No! You rushed into this thing,
didn't think it through,

848
00:53:02,875 --> 00:53:04,875
and now we're both in the hole.

849
00:53:05,917 --> 00:53:07,292
You're never gonna learn!

850
00:53:08,208 --> 00:53:11,667
- What are you talking about?
- You've been the same since we were kids!

851
00:53:11,750 --> 00:53:15,042
- Leap before you look. Every time!
- What does that mean? This restaurant.

852
00:53:15,125 --> 00:53:17,625
This is me trying.
I'm trying. Take a look.

853
00:53:17,708 --> 00:53:20,417
Oh, no. This whole thing is a joke, Joe!

854
00:53:20,500 --> 00:53:23,250
You really made your ma proud this time!

855
00:53:29,917 --> 00:53:30,917
Yeah?

856
00:53:32,083 --> 00:53:33,375
Go ahead and get out.

857
00:53:35,167 --> 00:53:37,542
I didn't… I didn't mean it like that.

858
00:53:38,625 --> 00:53:41,000
I'll pay your money back. All right?

859
00:53:42,417 --> 00:53:43,750
I want you to get out.

860
00:53:47,667 --> 00:53:48,667
Fine.

861
00:53:51,083 --> 00:53:52,125
Forget it.

862
00:53:52,667 --> 00:53:53,833
Forget you.

863
00:54:18,667 --> 00:54:21,042
Thank you for coming over so last minute.

864
00:54:21,125 --> 00:54:22,542
I really do appreciate your help.

865
00:54:22,625 --> 00:54:25,750
Oh, don't thank me yet.
I'm not sure we're gonna find anything.

866
00:54:25,833 --> 00:54:28,375
- Building codes are not my specialty.
- Yeah.

867
00:54:28,458 --> 00:54:30,750
Something's better than nothing.

868
00:54:30,833 --> 00:54:34,583
This is really the only chance I got,
so thank you.

869
00:54:35,875 --> 00:54:39,500
Your place.
This is where you lived with your mom.

870
00:54:39,583 --> 00:54:43,542
Well, yeah. I mean, well, my mom,
she was downstairs with my nonna.

871
00:54:43,625 --> 00:54:47,333
So, I was kind of up here
kind of looking after her, but, um…

872
00:54:47,417 --> 00:54:48,958
Yeah, you know.

873
00:54:49,042 --> 00:54:51,625
It's nice. I'm starting to…

874
00:54:51,708 --> 00:54:55,125
Maybe I'll get around
to giving it a paint job or something.

875
00:54:55,208 --> 00:54:57,417
Thinking about some new furniture, maybe.

876
00:54:57,500 --> 00:55:00,750
Don't get rid of this chair.
That's a great chair.

877
00:55:03,375 --> 00:55:04,375
Ah!

878
00:55:16,958 --> 00:55:20,292
Christmas. Your nonna made
this exact soup on Christmas.

879
00:55:20,375 --> 00:55:23,333
That's right.
You and your family came over.

880
00:55:23,958 --> 00:55:26,625
Not everybody was nice to us
when we first moved here,

881
00:55:26,708 --> 00:55:30,083
but your mom and your nonna,
they always were.

882
00:55:30,167 --> 00:55:32,875
Yeah. Well, you were easy to be nice to.

883
00:55:35,167 --> 00:55:41,583
Which is why I feel even worse
about the way that I handled prom.

884
00:55:41,667 --> 00:55:44,708
- That was a million years ago. We're 100.
- I know, but it was terrible.

885
00:55:44,792 --> 00:55:47,250
I am such an idiot.
Do you know what I did?

886
00:55:47,333 --> 00:55:51,875
Bruno and all the guys, we made a pact
that we were gonna go sneak out, right?

887
00:55:51,958 --> 00:55:55,500
He had the booze, the parents' house,
and we lost track of time.

888
00:55:55,583 --> 00:55:57,458
I tried to come back, and then…

889
00:55:58,042 --> 00:56:00,083
Ah, the whole thing was just a mess.

890
00:56:00,167 --> 00:56:02,750
And, uh… by the time I got back,

891
00:56:04,042 --> 00:56:05,458
no Olivia.

892
00:56:06,208 --> 00:56:09,917
Anyway, I don't wanna make it awkward,
after all these years, bringing it up,

893
00:56:10,000 --> 00:56:12,167
but I did wanna say to you that I'm sorry.

894
00:56:12,750 --> 00:56:13,750
I am.

895
00:56:13,792 --> 00:56:14,792
Thank you.

896
00:56:15,500 --> 00:56:17,125
I appreciate the apology.

897
00:56:18,333 --> 00:56:20,333
- Well, salute.
- Salute.

898
00:56:22,542 --> 00:56:27,250
So the long, complicated version is
we don't have a certificate of occupancy.

899
00:56:27,333 --> 00:56:28,917
Well, can't you reapply?

900
00:56:29,875 --> 00:56:31,542
Well, I already have, but…

901
00:56:31,625 --> 00:56:35,167
- That could take weeks or even a year.
- Right.

902
00:56:35,250 --> 00:56:38,042
- We could all be dead by then.
- I tried everything I could.

903
00:56:38,125 --> 00:56:41,708
Olivia and I were looking
for different loopholes, but nothing.

904
00:56:41,792 --> 00:56:44,458
I don't wanna go back to what I was doing.

905
00:56:44,542 --> 00:56:45,792
What was that?

906
00:56:47,958 --> 00:56:49,000
Nothing.

907
00:56:55,750 --> 00:56:57,083
What is she doing?

908
00:56:57,958 --> 00:56:59,208
Is she having a stroke?

909
00:56:59,792 --> 00:57:01,500
Santo Padre Pio,

910
00:57:02,542 --> 00:57:05,125
truly, I tell you.

911
00:57:07,208 --> 00:57:09,708
Ask, and it will be given.

912
00:57:09,792 --> 00:57:12,583
Seek, and you will be found.

913
00:57:13,167 --> 00:57:14,708
Bless these women.

914
00:57:14,792 --> 00:57:17,833
They have generations
of family in their heart.

915
00:57:19,583 --> 00:57:24,125
And bless Joe, because he has a dream.

916
00:57:25,417 --> 00:57:26,417
Bless us.

917
00:57:27,458 --> 00:57:31,250
In the name of the Father,
the Son, and the Holy Ghost.

918
00:57:41,375 --> 00:57:42,583
Now we wait.

919
00:57:46,625 --> 00:57:48,375
Uh, Teresa?

920
00:57:48,458 --> 00:57:50,625
What exactly are we waiting for?

921
00:57:51,958 --> 00:57:53,292
A miracle.

922
00:57:56,500 --> 00:57:57,500
Okay.

923
00:58:00,667 --> 00:58:01,667
Hey, Joe.

924
00:58:02,542 --> 00:58:04,125
I think you, uh, remember Phil.

925
00:58:04,208 --> 00:58:06,792
Yeah, I know… Phil. Wow.

926
00:58:06,875 --> 00:58:07,917
Phil?

927
00:58:08,792 --> 00:58:12,917
Mr. Scaravella,
I'm so sorry for the misunderstanding.

928
00:58:13,000 --> 00:58:15,583
Here is your, uh,
certificate of occupancy.

929
00:58:15,667 --> 00:58:18,875
If you could just do us a favor
and, uh, get that wall fixed

930
00:58:18,958 --> 00:58:21,875
and that, uh, oven replaced,
we'd really appreciate it.

931
00:58:21,958 --> 00:58:24,417
Sorry for the inconvenience.
Have a good day, everyone.

932
00:58:24,500 --> 00:58:25,417
Oh!

933
00:58:25,500 --> 00:58:27,000
I don't understand.

934
00:58:27,083 --> 00:58:29,417
The place we didn't look
was Better Business Bureau.

935
00:58:29,500 --> 00:58:31,125
Phil here, he's had 53 complaints.

936
00:58:31,208 --> 00:58:33,000
You have to bribe him in order

937
00:58:33,083 --> 00:58:34,764
to come back
and do a follow-up inspection.

938
00:58:34,833 --> 00:58:37,042
- You can't prove any of that.
- I can, and I will.

939
00:58:37,125 --> 00:58:38,583
How dare you?

940
00:58:38,667 --> 00:58:42,208
- Get outta here!
- Fix the wall. Get a new oven.

941
00:58:42,292 --> 00:58:43,542
Yes, consider it done.

942
00:58:43,625 --> 00:58:45,792
- Beat it!
- God forgives you.

943
00:58:49,875 --> 00:58:52,250
I told you so. A lawyer!

944
00:58:52,333 --> 00:58:53,750
Oh, stop!

945
00:58:54,250 --> 00:58:56,333
Brava!

946
00:58:56,417 --> 00:58:58,167
Hey. Thank you.

947
00:58:58,250 --> 00:59:00,250
- It's good news.
- Brava!

948
00:59:12,417 --> 00:59:14,833
Be good. Say the rosary.

949
00:59:14,917 --> 00:59:16,750
Okay. Say it for me, please.

950
00:59:29,125 --> 00:59:30,542
- Hey.
- Hey. Here you go.

951
00:59:30,625 --> 00:59:32,750
- It took you long enough.
- Sorry about that.

952
00:59:32,833 --> 00:59:34,458
- Aren't you gonna come in?
- Sure.

953
00:59:34,542 --> 00:59:35,542
Come on.

954
00:59:39,583 --> 00:59:42,750
Close the door, please.
You're letting in a draft.

955
00:59:43,542 --> 00:59:45,292
- Yeah.
- No... Joe.

956
00:59:45,375 --> 00:59:47,917
Go sit down. You two have to talk.

957
00:59:49,000 --> 00:59:50,042
Come on.

958
00:59:55,833 --> 00:59:58,375
Look, your friend brought you zeppole.

959
00:59:59,042 --> 01:00:00,042
Talk.

960
01:00:00,625 --> 01:00:02,125
I'm staying out of it.

961
01:00:12,083 --> 01:00:15,167
Clearly, there was mistakes
made on your part.

