1209
01:13:31,000 --> 01:13:34,542
Yes. There was one once.

1210
01:13:35,417 --> 01:13:37,250
Hmm?

1211
01:13:40,500 --> 01:13:42,125
What was his name?

1212
01:13:45,625 --> 01:13:46,625
Isabella.

1213
01:13:48,917 --> 01:13:49,958
Yeah, Isabella.

1214
01:13:51,250 --> 01:13:52,250
What happened?

1215
01:13:52,292 --> 01:13:54,500
Nothing. Nothing happened.

1216
01:13:54,583 --> 01:13:57,458
It was a sin. I left the convent.

1217
01:13:57,542 --> 01:13:59,417
And that's when... Oh.

1218
01:13:59,500 --> 01:14:04,292
It's not easy to live in a world
that rejects what you are.

1219
01:14:04,375 --> 01:14:05,375
Yes.

1220
01:14:06,625 --> 01:14:07,750
Oh, my God.

1221
01:14:07,833 --> 01:14:09,125
That's terrible.

1222
01:14:11,458 --> 01:14:14,042
No, no. Here. To Isabella.

1223
01:14:14,125 --> 01:14:15,917
- To Isabella.
- Isabella.

1224
01:14:16,000 --> 01:14:17,500
- Isabella.
- To you, honey.

1225
01:14:18,667 --> 01:14:20,458
- To you.
- You deserve it.

1226
01:14:20,542 --> 01:14:21,750
Thank you all.

1227
01:14:21,833 --> 01:14:22,667
To you.

1228
01:14:22,750 --> 01:14:23,792
And Teresa.

1229
01:14:23,875 --> 01:14:26,208
- Bless you, darling.
- Oh.

1230
01:14:26,292 --> 01:14:27,292
Hmm.

1231
01:14:28,500 --> 01:14:29,542
Hmm.

1232
01:14:33,875 --> 01:14:37,375
And what about your family, Antonella?

1233
01:14:37,458 --> 01:14:41,792
Well, my Gianni
has been gone for many years.

1234
01:14:43,667 --> 01:14:46,792
But we had three beautiful children.

1235
01:14:46,875 --> 01:14:49,208
They live all over the country now.

1236
01:14:49,292 --> 01:14:50,667
Nine grandchildren.

1237
01:14:50,750 --> 01:14:52,000
Beautiful.

1238
01:14:52,083 --> 01:14:54,458
I don't see them very often,

1239
01:14:55,833 --> 01:14:59,167
but I'm very proud of them because
they're living their lives very well.

1240
01:14:59,250 --> 01:15:01,333
And that makes me very happy.

1241
01:15:02,333 --> 01:15:06,375
And, uh, thank you for today,
because this has been great, hasn't it?

1242
01:15:06,458 --> 01:15:09,667
- Here's to living our lives very well.
- Indeed.

1243
01:15:09,750 --> 01:15:11,208
- Yes, yes.
- Indeed!

1244
01:15:11,292 --> 01:15:12,125
Yes.

1245
01:15:12,208 --> 01:15:15,542
- So good.
- I've never stayed up all night.

1246
01:15:39,875 --> 01:15:42,375
- Gorgeous!
- Wow!

1247
01:15:42,458 --> 01:15:43,458
Grazie!

1248
01:15:43,500 --> 01:15:45,833
Look at these. You guys look beautiful.

1249
01:15:45,917 --> 01:15:47,917
Grazie!

1250
01:15:48,708 --> 01:15:54,208
- You can thank Gia for this.
- It's not the painter. It's the canvas.

1251
01:15:54,292 --> 01:15:58,000
I got drunk, but I don't have a hangover
because I had water.

1252
01:15:58,083 --> 01:15:59,333
Smart!

1253
01:16:06,042 --> 01:16:08,875
Hey, Joe, tonight we feed the world.

1254
01:16:08,958 --> 01:16:10,667
- Sì?
- Se!

1255
01:16:12,750 --> 01:16:14,500
Whoo!

1256
01:16:19,125 --> 01:16:20,500
It's showtime!

1257
01:16:28,750 --> 01:16:30,792
Opening night and we get a thunderstorm.

1258
01:16:34,375 --> 01:16:37,542
Hey, sorry we're late.
It's crazy weather out there.

1259
01:16:37,625 --> 01:16:40,458
- God.
- There she is. Our legal counsel.

1260
01:16:40,542 --> 01:16:42,000
Look at you.

1261
01:16:42,083 --> 01:16:45,333
- It's like we're back in high school.
- Oh, you wish you were in high school.

1262
01:16:45,417 --> 01:16:47,542
- Hello. Oh!
- Hello.

1263
01:16:47,625 --> 01:16:52,333
Oh, my God, Joe.
It really looks beautiful. Hmm.

1264
01:16:52,417 --> 01:16:53,542
Yeah.

1265
01:16:56,333 --> 01:16:59,125
You. You did good, you. Come here.

1266
01:16:59,208 --> 01:17:01,958
Yeah, it was nothing. Now, hey.

1267
01:17:03,250 --> 01:17:05,125
- For good luck, brother.
- Hey.

1268
01:17:05,208 --> 01:17:08,417
Thanks so much for coming, guys.
It's great seeing you.

1269
01:17:08,500 --> 01:17:09,875
Nice.

1270
01:17:12,375 --> 01:17:14,667
So is the, uh, dinner rush over?

1271
01:17:14,750 --> 01:17:17,333
Over?

1272
01:17:17,417 --> 01:17:20,833
- It didn't start yet.
- Yeah, it's been kinda slow.

1273
01:17:22,375 --> 01:17:23,375
How slow?

1274
01:17:24,042 --> 01:17:27,042
You are actually
our first customers tonight, so…

1275
01:17:27,125 --> 01:17:29,875
Joey, my brother, and his family,
they were gonna come here,

1276
01:17:29,958 --> 01:17:33,417
but I think they're afraid
of getting stuck in the storm.

1277
01:17:33,500 --> 01:17:35,458
They're from Philadelphia, so…

1278
01:17:36,250 --> 01:17:39,583
You know what? Here's the good news.
We got two lovely customers.

1279
01:17:39,667 --> 01:17:42,250
Let's give 'em an experience
they'll never forget, right?

1280
01:17:42,333 --> 01:17:43,167
- Right!
- Yes!

1281
01:17:43,250 --> 01:17:45,917
- Spoil 'em!
- I'll show you to your table.

1282
01:17:46,000 --> 01:17:47,000
All right.

1283
01:17:48,000 --> 01:17:50,667
So… Does this mean we have to pay?

1284
01:17:50,750 --> 01:17:52,917
Absolutely. Thank you so much for coming.

1285
01:17:53,000 --> 01:17:54,000
Okay…

1286
01:17:55,917 --> 01:17:57,042
Hmm.

1287
01:17:59,542 --> 01:18:02,417
Ladies, you have completely
outdone yourselves.

1288
01:18:03,292 --> 01:18:05,792
This is the greatest meal I've had since…

1289
01:18:05,875 --> 01:18:06,875
last night.

1290
01:18:07,833 --> 01:18:11,667
Truly. This really is
the best Italian cooking I have ever had.

1291
01:18:16,083 --> 01:18:17,375
Yeah, it's, uh…

1292
01:18:18,417 --> 01:18:21,167
It's getting kinda late.
I think we should call it here,

1293
01:18:21,250 --> 01:18:24,917
but, uh, terrific job. It's great.

1294
01:19:42,542 --> 01:19:43,583
If you're around…

1295
01:20:10,292 --> 01:20:12,750
Thank you, Aunt Teresa.

1296
01:20:15,292 --> 01:20:16,875
Thank you for coming.

1297
01:20:16,958 --> 01:20:18,833
Thank you for coming.

1298
01:20:52,375 --> 01:20:54,375
There we go. Here's the news.

1299
01:20:54,458 --> 01:20:55,542
- For you.
- Joe!

1300
01:20:55,625 --> 01:21:00,125
- These are your paychecks.
- The restaurant hasn't earned a dime.

1301
01:21:00,208 --> 01:21:02,625
- Wait until things kick in, that's crazy.
- Absolutely not.

1302
01:21:02,708 --> 01:21:05,125
Every two weeks, you get a check.
It's been two weeks.

1303
01:21:05,208 --> 01:21:07,875
You're not working here for free.
That's your money, okay?

1304
01:21:07,958 --> 01:21:09,458
We'll figure it out.

1305
01:21:09,542 --> 01:21:11,875
- Joe.
- Why isn't anyone coming?

1306
01:21:13,500 --> 01:21:16,333
- Shame on you!
- Hey, what'd you do that for?

1307
01:21:16,417 --> 01:21:19,583
You're telling people not to come?
Is that what you're doing?

1308
01:21:20,167 --> 01:21:21,542
It ain't just me.

1309
01:21:21,625 --> 01:21:24,375
The entire neighborhood
wants that place gone.

1310
01:21:24,458 --> 01:21:26,167
I don't like that he's not from here,

1311
01:21:26,250 --> 01:21:28,750
and I don't like how
he's using you ladies as a gimmick.

1312
01:21:28,833 --> 01:21:30,250
Using me as a gimmick?

1313
01:21:30,333 --> 01:21:34,708
He's not using me!
He's celebrating me, youstunad.

1314
01:21:34,792 --> 01:21:36,667
- Come on.
- How dare you? How dare you?

1315
01:21:36,750 --> 01:21:38,417
- Antonella, hey!
- Shut up.

1316
01:21:38,500 --> 01:21:40,708
- Antonella, hey! Vieni cà.
- Leave me alone.

1317
01:21:42,667 --> 01:21:44,250
Joe's a good man.

1318
01:21:44,333 --> 01:21:47,708
He's not trying to take anything away.
He's trying to give something back.

1319
01:21:50,792 --> 01:21:51,792
Night, Joe.

1320
01:21:52,333 --> 01:21:53,792
- Good night.
- Night, Joe.

1321
01:21:53,875 --> 01:21:55,292
- Night.
- Good night, Joe.

1322
01:21:55,375 --> 01:21:57,125
- Night, Joe.
- See you later.

1323
01:21:57,208 --> 01:21:59,000
- Have a good night.
- Good night, Joey.

1324
01:21:59,083 --> 01:22:01,042
- How was class?
- It was good.

1325
01:22:01,125 --> 01:22:02,333
That's good.

1326
01:22:13,292 --> 01:22:15,708
So, how bad?

1327
01:22:16,458 --> 01:22:18,375
I think it's all over but the crying.

1328
01:22:18,458 --> 01:22:22,250
I've done everything I can think of.
I can't get anyone to come down here.

1329
01:22:22,333 --> 01:22:25,750
I've called the critics,
emailed the critics. I've done it twice.

1330
01:22:25,833 --> 01:22:29,833
I'm gonna end up on a restraining order
from some of these guys.

1331
01:22:29,917 --> 01:22:33,625
So, I was gonna wait and maybe,
you know, tomorrow,

1332
01:22:34,583 --> 01:22:37,750
just let everyone know there's no way
to keep this place open anymore.

1333
01:22:37,833 --> 01:22:40,708
Oh. No, no, no, you can't say that.

1334
01:22:43,625 --> 01:22:45,958
Wait a minute. If they won't come here,

1335
01:22:47,667 --> 01:22:50,625
maybe you should… you should go there.

1336
01:22:51,125 --> 01:22:52,208
Take it to them.

1337
01:22:53,667 --> 01:22:54,500
Maybe.

1338
01:22:54,583 --> 01:22:55,625
Oh, come on.

1339
01:22:56,458 --> 01:22:57,333
Sweetie,

1340
01:22:57,417 --> 01:23:00,708
the only thing at the end of the day
that you're gonna regret

1341
01:23:00,792 --> 01:23:04,000
are not the mistakes you make.
You can make your peace and move on.

1342
01:23:04,083 --> 01:23:08,042
You're gonna regret
the moments that you did not take,

1343
01:23:08,125 --> 01:23:10,750
and this is your moment, Joe.

1344
01:23:47,500 --> 01:23:48,958
- Mr. Durant?
- Oh?

1345
01:23:49,833 --> 01:23:50,875
Hi.

1346
01:23:50,958 --> 01:23:51,958
Uh, no.

1347
01:23:52,292 --> 01:23:56,583
Oh, let me start off by saying it's wildly
inappropriate to come barging in on you.

1348
01:23:56,667 --> 01:23:58,167
- My apologies.
- Who are you?

1349
01:23:58,250 --> 01:24:02,042
- I'm sorry. I'm Joe Scaravella.
- You can't just walk in. What's going on?

1350
01:24:02,125 --> 01:24:04,167
- I'm not walking in.
- I'm gonna call security.

1351
01:24:04,250 --> 01:24:07,083
- I'm opening an Italian restaurant.
- Hey, Michael.

1352
01:24:07,167 --> 01:24:09,917
Instead of hiring professional chefs…

1353
01:24:10,000 --> 01:24:11,833
- Taylor?
- …I hired nonnas to do the cooking.

1354
01:24:11,917 --> 01:24:12,833
Sure.

1355
01:24:12,917 --> 01:24:16,750
When people come in, I wanted them
to feel like when they were younger

1356
01:24:16,833 --> 01:24:19,875
and have the person who loved them
the very most in their life cook for them.

1357
01:24:20,458 --> 01:24:24,083
- Grandmothers are cooking for you?
- Yes, Italian grandmothers.

1358
01:24:24,167 --> 01:24:27,458
Uh-huh.
Are you some kind of insane person?

1359
01:24:27,542 --> 01:24:29,833
I'm a little bit crazy,
but not in a scary way.

1360
01:24:29,917 --> 01:24:32,958
Just passionate about food,
and I wanted to share this with you.

1361
01:24:33,042 --> 01:24:35,917
- No, don't...
- Can I just show you these dishes?

1362
01:24:36,000 --> 01:24:38,500
Look at this. This isstrangolapreti.

1363
01:24:38,583 --> 01:24:41,250
This right here, this has heirloom.

1364
01:24:41,333 --> 01:24:43,375
- Oh, my God.
- It has spinach, right?

1365
01:24:43,458 --> 01:24:45,083
- Ricotta.
- Oh boy.

1366
01:24:45,167 --> 01:24:47,542
Burro fusoand sage. It's just simple.

1367
01:24:47,625 --> 01:24:51,000
All from all different places in Italy
made by all different nonnas,

1368
01:24:51,083 --> 01:24:53,458
and they have cannolis here for dessert.

1369
01:24:53,542 --> 01:24:57,208
And it's all homemade.
All from nonnas. All from the grandmas.

1370
01:24:58,292 --> 01:24:59,292
All right.

1371
01:25:00,542 --> 01:25:01,667
Enoteca Maria.

1372
01:25:01,750 --> 01:25:03,708
Yes, Enoteca Maria, after my mom.

1373
01:25:05,833 --> 01:25:06,708
Staten Island.

1374
01:25:06,792 --> 01:25:07,958
Yes.

1375
01:25:08,583 --> 01:25:09,583
Um…

1376
01:25:10,542 --> 01:25:12,667
Yeah, Joe,

1377
01:25:12,750 --> 01:25:16,000
you realize I review restaurants
here in Manhattan.

1378
01:25:16,083 --> 01:25:21,375
You know, three-star, two-star, one-star
Michelin restaurants here and abroad.

1379
01:25:21,458 --> 01:25:23,417
Exactly. And that's why I'm here.

1380
01:25:23,500 --> 01:25:27,958
If you could, I'd love if you could review
Enoteca Maria this weekend.

1381
01:25:31,250 --> 01:25:34,208
Well, this weekend…

1382
01:25:34,292 --> 01:25:39,042
I am booked up until January.

1383
01:25:42,750 --> 01:25:46,500
So, next time you decide
to open a restaurant, maybe…

1384
01:25:47,750 --> 01:25:49,000
Plan better.

1385
01:25:49,792 --> 01:25:51,042
I can admit that.

1386
01:25:51,125 --> 01:25:53,417
There isn't a great business plan
in place for this place.

1387
01:25:53,500 --> 01:25:54,792
You're right about that.

1388
01:25:54,875 --> 01:25:57,500
But I do have a really good plan
for the restaurant.

1389
01:25:58,458 --> 01:26:00,042
Okay, 'cause it's not a restaurant.

1390
01:26:00,125 --> 01:26:03,958
It's really more about family,
and experiencing family.

1391
01:26:04,042 --> 01:26:07,167
Especially for people
who may not have family anymore.

1392
01:26:07,250 --> 01:26:10,250
The nonnas that are doing the cooking,
they're tremendous chefs.

1393
01:26:10,333 --> 01:26:13,000
I'm not coming in here
asking you to do us a favor.

1394
01:26:13,083 --> 01:26:16,417
I just want you to come down
and experience the restaurant

1395
01:26:16,500 --> 01:26:18,208
and just give it a fair shot.

1396
01:26:18,792 --> 01:26:20,458
I think it's pretty special.

1397
01:26:25,375 --> 01:26:27,375
- Pick up, pick up, pick up.
- Don't worry.

1398
01:26:27,458 --> 01:26:29,000
Pick up, pick up, pick up.

1399
01:26:29,083 --> 01:26:31,833
Ah, straight to voicemail, again.

1400
01:26:36,542 --> 01:26:39,250
I hope Joe's okay. That he's not hurt.

1401
01:26:39,333 --> 01:26:42,792
That he didn't fall or hurt his leg.
Maybe he's in the street.

1402
01:26:43,458 --> 01:26:46,125
Joe isn't hurt. He's just not showing up.

1403
01:26:46,625 --> 01:26:48,958
Oh, I know what you're saying.

1404
01:26:49,042 --> 01:26:51,000
And I don't like it.

1405
01:26:51,083 --> 01:26:53,333
Joe will be here!

1406
01:26:53,417 --> 01:26:54,417
Really?

1407
01:26:55,083 --> 01:26:56,167
What did I say?

1408
01:26:56,958 --> 01:27:01,583
No one cares about us,
about our cooking, about our stories.

1409
01:27:01,667 --> 01:27:02,583
Nobody cares.

1410
01:27:02,667 --> 01:27:06,083
We are discarded old artifacts.
Do you understand?

1411
01:27:06,167 --> 01:27:09,375
- That's what we are.
- Uh-uh-uh. You speak for yourself, woman.

1412
01:27:09,458 --> 01:27:12,958
- I don't believe that's true.
- We've been open for more than a month.

1413
01:27:13,042 --> 01:27:17,208
Who has come in other than
friends and family? We're unimportant.

1414
01:27:17,792 --> 01:27:19,958
Insignificant.

1415
01:27:20,042 --> 01:27:23,417
And no one is gonna
remember us for anything.

1416
01:27:23,500 --> 01:27:25,417
Okay. See the door?

1417
01:27:25,500 --> 01:27:28,333
Don't let it hit you
in the ass on the way out!

1418
01:27:28,417 --> 01:27:30,542
Because I'm something here!

1419
01:27:31,167 --> 01:27:32,833
This means something to me!

1420
01:27:32,917 --> 01:27:37,250
I'm not discarded,
and I don't feel discarded like you feel!

1421
01:27:37,333 --> 01:27:41,292
- Don't start with me. Enough already.
- Get out! We don't need you!

1422
01:27:41,375 --> 01:27:44,458
Silenzio! Please! I'm so ashamed of you.

1423
01:27:44,542 --> 01:27:48,500
We are not quitters. We do not walk away.

1424
01:27:48,583 --> 01:27:51,042
We're intelligent, strong women.

1425
01:27:51,125 --> 01:27:55,750
We're beautiful women
with Italian blood in our souls.

1426
01:27:55,833 --> 01:28:01,875
And we've been through too much together,
and I'm not gonna let this end in anger.

1427
01:28:03,292 --> 01:28:04,417
Well said.

1428
01:28:06,375 --> 01:28:07,917
Grazie.

1429
01:28:09,958 --> 01:28:11,167
All right.

1430
01:28:15,042 --> 01:28:17,458
- Okay.
- Okay, Bologna, come on.

1431
01:28:21,667 --> 01:28:22,792
Hey.

1432
01:28:22,875 --> 01:28:24,000
- Joe!
- How are you?

1433
01:28:24,083 --> 01:28:25,333
Hey, Joe.

1434
01:28:25,417 --> 01:28:27,125
- Hi.
- Hey.

1435
01:28:28,042 --> 01:28:30,833
Okay, whatever it is, it's gonna be okay.

1436
01:28:30,917 --> 01:28:32,750
I appreciate that.

1437
01:28:32,833 --> 01:28:33,833
Uh…

1438
01:28:34,750 --> 01:28:40,500
Well, honestly, I wish I had better news
because you guys were all terrific.

1439
01:28:40,583 --> 01:28:41,417
Honestly.

1440
01:28:41,500 --> 01:28:45,417
And you all definitely deserve
to keep this thing going.

1441
01:28:45,500 --> 01:28:46,500
Um…

1442
01:28:47,083 --> 01:28:52,000
You know, I think it's safe to say no one
wanted this thing to fly more than I did.

1443
01:28:52,083 --> 01:28:54,750
You know, not just for myself,
but for my mom.

1444
01:28:55,375 --> 01:28:58,083
But also, really, because of all of you.

1445
01:28:58,167 --> 01:29:01,708
And just how special
and how much you all mean to me.

1446
01:29:01,792 --> 01:29:03,000
But, uh…

1447
01:29:04,208 --> 01:29:08,833
The truth is, we're just not gonna
be able to keep these doors open.

1448
01:29:09,875 --> 01:29:13,042
And I say thank you and I'm sorry.

1449
01:29:15,125 --> 01:29:16,167
You…

1450
01:29:16,250 --> 01:29:20,458
You gave it your best shot.
And we're very proud of you.

1451
01:29:22,583 --> 01:29:23,833
You did good.

1452
01:29:23,917 --> 01:29:26,208
We all did our best, Joe.

1453
01:29:27,792 --> 01:29:29,833
Your mother would be proud.

1454
01:29:32,500 --> 01:29:33,417
Thank you.

1455
01:29:33,500 --> 01:29:34,667
She would.

1456
01:29:34,750 --> 01:29:35,833
Yeah.

1457
01:29:36,375 --> 01:29:40,125
You know what?
Now we're all like a family. Right?

1458
01:29:40,958 --> 01:29:43,917
So, if that's the one thing
that we get outta this,

1459
01:29:44,625 --> 01:29:47,083
then I think we've won. So, thank you.

1460
01:29:47,167 --> 01:29:48,333
Thank you.

1461
01:29:53,708 --> 01:29:54,542
Yeah.

1462
01:29:54,625 --> 01:29:57,750
"The family you choose."

1463
01:29:58,542 --> 01:29:59,750
That's us.

1464
01:30:07,125 --> 01:30:10,708
Oh, we got a problem.
We have a lot of food in that kitchen.

1465
01:30:10,792 --> 01:30:12,958
It would be a sin to throw it away, Joe.

1466
01:30:13,958 --> 01:30:15,208
Well, let's not.

1467
01:30:15,292 --> 01:30:18,792
Why don't we invite our family,
our friends, anyone we know,

1468
01:30:18,875 --> 01:30:21,125
and let's have one hell
of a Sunday night dinner?

1469
01:30:21,208 --> 01:30:23,125
- Yes!
- Great idea.

1470
01:30:23,208 --> 01:30:25,250
- Yes, a party.
- Am I right?

1471
01:30:25,333 --> 01:30:28,125
- Yes!
- With Limoncello!

1472
01:30:28,208 --> 01:30:29,208
- No!
- No!

1473
01:30:33,833 --> 01:30:38,417
- Wingman showed up. Nice to see you.
- Nice to see you. Good to see you.

1474
01:30:38,500 --> 01:30:42,375
- This is Olivia. These are my MTA guys.
- Vito. Nice to meet you.

1475
01:30:42,458 --> 01:30:46,500
- You guys sit wherever you want, okay?
- We're doing it family style.

1476
01:30:46,583 --> 01:30:51,833
- Say hi to cousin Tammy. Cousin Tammy!
- Hi! It's so nice to meet you!

1477
01:30:51,917 --> 01:30:55,625
- You look great. Nice to see you.
- Thank you. This is beautiful.

1478
01:30:55,708 --> 01:30:59,083
- Beautiful. My man, good to see you.
- Congrats.

1479
01:30:59,167 --> 01:31:00,417
Hey.

1480
01:31:00,500 --> 01:31:02,750
I just wanna let you know,
as soon as I sell the place,

1481
01:31:02,833 --> 01:31:04,233
I'm gonna pay you back every penny.

1482
01:31:04,292 --> 01:31:08,417
Hey, stop it. No. Tonight's about you.
None of that stuff matters.

1483
01:31:08,500 --> 01:31:10,708
Yeah. Come on, we're proud of you.

1484
01:31:10,792 --> 01:31:14,583
- Wanna show them where they're sitting?
- I'm starving. Come on.

1485
01:31:15,542 --> 01:31:18,208
Hey, you made it.
Thanks so much for coming.

1486
01:31:18,292 --> 01:31:19,708
- You look terrific.
- Joey.

1487
01:31:19,792 --> 01:31:21,917
Good to see you. Glad you're here tonight.

1488
01:31:23,792 --> 01:31:25,667
- Hey.
- Hey.

1489
01:31:25,750 --> 01:31:27,208
Uh…

1490
01:31:27,292 --> 01:31:30,833
I heard this is your last night.
I'm sorry about that.

1491
01:31:30,917 --> 01:31:35,750
I'm a businessman too,
and I wouldn't wish that on anybody, so…

1492
01:31:39,500 --> 01:31:41,333
It's a, you know, kind of an homage.

1493
01:31:41,417 --> 01:31:43,792
Part of the history of the building,
so we kept it.

1494
01:31:47,042 --> 01:31:49,542
It's beautiful. Thank you.

1495
01:31:49,625 --> 01:31:50,750
Well…

1496
01:31:50,833 --> 01:31:53,750
I… This is for you.
I'm just gonna take off.

1497
01:31:53,833 --> 01:31:56,833
No, no, no, sit down.
Have some food, crack this open,

1498
01:31:56,917 --> 01:32:00,917
I'll come and share a glass with ya, okay?
Come sit down and eat. Come in.

1499
01:32:06,875 --> 01:32:11,375
There's a lot of people out there
waiting to experience your hearts. Ready?

1500
01:32:11,458 --> 01:32:13,792
- Yes!
- Let's go!

1501
01:32:13,875 --> 01:32:16,208
- Ready!
- Okay.

1502
01:32:31,958 --> 01:32:33,208
That's a lot of salt!

1503
01:32:33,292 --> 01:32:34,750
- Coming up.
- Pour it.

1504
01:32:36,083 --> 01:32:38,625
Those look so good. Delicious!

1505
01:32:44,125 --> 01:32:45,458
Here, try this.

1506
01:32:47,292 --> 01:32:49,042
Hmm!

1507
01:32:57,083 --> 01:32:58,083
Okay, baby.

1508
01:32:59,167 --> 01:33:01,208
So good. Oh, my God.

1509
01:33:10,292 --> 01:33:11,292
Oh, my God.

1510
01:33:16,000 --> 01:33:17,917
Pass this down.

1511
01:33:42,708 --> 01:33:43,958
Hey!

1512
01:33:46,583 --> 01:33:50,167
- Our nonnas would be proud.
- To our nonnas.

1513
01:33:50,250 --> 01:33:51,333
To the nonnas.

1514
01:33:55,667 --> 01:33:56,833
Excuse me.

1515
01:33:56,917 --> 01:33:59,667
Could you guys
all come out here for a second, please?

1516
01:34:04,833 --> 01:34:06,000
What'd we do?

1517
01:34:08,500 --> 01:34:09,500
All right.

1518
01:34:25,792 --> 01:34:27,250
Yeah!

1519
01:34:33,625 --> 01:34:35,167
Great job.

1520
01:37:25,833 --> 01:37:26,958
Hmm.

1521
01:38:30,167 --> 01:38:31,167
What's happening?

1522
01:38:31,750 --> 01:38:32,750
Well…

1523
01:38:41,083 --> 01:38:43,833
Well, I'm sorry to interrupt,
and I appreciate your time.

1524
01:38:44,500 --> 01:38:45,500
Thank you.

1525
01:39:08,167 --> 01:39:12,917
When my editor, Edward Durant,
asked me to review Enoteca Maria,

1526
01:39:13,000 --> 01:39:18,125
a new Italian restaurant located at
27 Hyatt Street, Staten Island, New York,

1527
01:39:18,208 --> 01:39:21,208
I was compelled to see
what hiring real-life nonnas

1528
01:39:21,292 --> 01:39:23,375
instead of established chefs
was all about.

1529
01:39:24,417 --> 01:39:26,292
But what I would soon discover

1530
01:39:26,375 --> 01:39:30,292
is that this quaint, little,
beautifully designed restaurant,

1531
01:39:30,375 --> 01:39:32,750
with a warm and inviting decor,

1532
01:39:32,833 --> 01:39:35,250
served up far more
than just delicious food.

1533
01:39:35,917 --> 01:39:37,458
It served family.

1534
01:39:38,583 --> 01:39:41,000
That's great!

1535
01:39:41,083 --> 01:39:42,708
- You did it, brother.
- We did it.

1536
01:39:42,792 --> 01:39:44,875
Beautifully designed, huh? Come on.

1537
01:39:47,417 --> 01:39:51,292
It served culture and history.

1538
01:39:54,083 --> 01:39:55,500
Attaboy, Joey!

1539
01:39:55,583 --> 01:39:59,667
It served generations worth
of traditions and stories.

1540
01:40:03,667 --> 01:40:07,750
So if you want just great food,
don't go to Enoteca Maria.

1541
01:40:07,833 --> 01:40:11,708
But if you want great food
that not only fills your stomach,

1542
01:40:11,792 --> 01:40:16,042
but will lift your soul,
then run, don't walk,

1543
01:40:16,125 --> 01:40:18,292
to a little slice of family

1544
01:40:18,375 --> 01:40:21,250
where you can let the one person
who loved you most in life

1545
01:40:21,333 --> 01:40:23,333
cook for you again.

1546
01:40:24,083 --> 01:40:26,500
And definitely order thecapuzzelle.

1547
01:40:32,583 --> 01:40:33,583
Hello?

1548
01:40:35,208 --> 01:40:36,542
Sadie?

1549
01:40:36,625 --> 01:40:37,917
Yes, this is Sadie.

1550
01:40:39,125 --> 01:40:40,333
It's Mama.

1551
01:40:41,917 --> 01:40:42,958
Ma?

1552
01:40:43,042 --> 01:40:44,333
Yeah.

1553
01:40:44,417 --> 01:40:47,000
Hi. Is everything okay?

1554
01:40:47,083 --> 01:40:48,083
Yeah.

1555
01:40:52,417 --> 01:40:54,542
Everybody was skeptical, but not me.

1556
01:40:54,625 --> 01:40:57,625
I said I would design this place,
and now look at what's going on here.

1557
01:40:57,708 --> 01:41:01,208
- "This is beautifully designed."
- Can I borrow you for a second, please?

1558
01:41:01,292 --> 01:41:04,208
All right, let's reload here.
Everything good?

1559
01:41:04,292 --> 01:41:06,083
- Amazing.
- Counselor?

1560
01:41:06,167 --> 01:41:08,542
- Look. You did this all.
- You kidding me? We did this.

1561
01:41:08,625 --> 01:41:11,833
Please. We need to hire another server,
because I got finals.

1562
01:41:12,875 --> 01:41:16,208
Again with the flowers?
Take a day off. Let her miss you.

1563
01:41:16,292 --> 01:41:19,333
- How's it going? Everything good?
- Couldn't be better, tesoro.

1564
01:41:19,417 --> 01:41:22,333
- What's the news, Magical?
- I'm in a wool sweater!

1565
01:41:22,417 --> 01:41:25,292
I'm sorry with the sheep's head
and the eyes, but it is selling.

1566
01:41:25,375 --> 01:41:27,735
- You have to admit, she's doing terrific.
- I'm working here.

1567
01:41:27,792 --> 01:41:30,417
I understand. I'll be right back.
I'm just gonna get some air.

1568
01:41:30,500 --> 01:41:32,208
- Have a good time, Joe.
- Yeah.

1569
01:41:32,292 --> 01:41:33,750
Proud of you guys.

1570
01:41:38,042 --> 01:41:40,625
I'll meet you any time you want

1571
01:41:41,167 --> 01:41:45,792
In our Italian restaurant

1572
01:43:30,417 --> 01:43:33,042
She took the ocean home to you

1573
01:43:34,167 --> 01:43:36,958
She saw the lady tall and true

1574
01:43:37,667 --> 01:43:41,917
She stood in line at Ellis Island
Wrote her name and took the highland

1575
01:43:42,000 --> 01:43:45,042
To the red, white and the blue

1576
01:43:45,917 --> 01:43:49,417
She found her dream of liberty

1577
01:43:49,500 --> 01:43:53,500
And what'd she give us? Italy!

1578
01:43:53,583 --> 01:43:56,292
She's our Nonna

1579
01:43:56,375 --> 01:43:59,417
She lived on Hyatt Street

1580
01:44:04,292 --> 01:44:07,333
She worked hard and found her joy

1581
01:44:08,167 --> 01:44:11,042
Then met a nice Italian boy

1582
01:44:12,000 --> 01:44:15,750
Her resolve, it never faltered
As they knelt there at the altar

1583
01:44:15,833 --> 01:44:19,583
And raised their little girl and boy

1584
01:44:19,667 --> 01:44:23,208
She found her dream of liberty

1585
01:44:23,292 --> 01:44:27,417
And what'd she give us? Italy!

1586
01:44:27,500 --> 01:44:30,042
She's our Nonna

1587
01:44:30,125 --> 01:44:34,458
She lived on Hyatt Street

1588
01:44:34,542 --> 01:44:38,333
So many dreams

1589
01:44:38,417 --> 01:44:41,708
So many names

1590
01:44:42,292 --> 01:44:45,542
We're all unique

1591
01:44:46,042 --> 01:44:49,542
And all the same

1592
01:44:49,625 --> 01:44:54,042
So for the millions of the faces

1593
01:44:54,125 --> 01:44:57,500
Who built the town
And left their traces

1594
01:44:57,583 --> 01:44:59,500
You're not alone

1595
01:44:59,583 --> 01:45:04,333
You've got a home on Hyatt Street

1596
01:45:05,958 --> 01:45:08,125
Buongiorno!

1597
01:45:08,208 --> 01:45:10,292
Arrivederci!

1598
01:45:10,375 --> 01:45:12,667
We took the ferry home to you

1599
01:45:13,917 --> 01:45:16,958
We saw the lady tall and true

1600
01:45:17,792 --> 01:45:21,750
We brought the kids to Ellis Island
Found your name and took the highland

1601
01:45:21,833 --> 01:45:25,375
To the red, white, and the blue

1602
01:45:25,458 --> 01:45:29,167
We are your dream of liberty

1603
01:45:29,250 --> 01:45:33,250
And what'd you give us? Italy!

1604
01:45:33,333 --> 01:45:36,000
You're our Nonna

1605
01:45:36,083 --> 01:45:39,875
You live on Hyatt
We can't deny it

1606
01:45:39,958 --> 01:45:42,750
It's never quiet Come home

1607
01:45:42,833 --> 01:45:49,833
To Hyatt Street